    thinking: "**Analyzing Environment Constraints**\n\nOkay, I\'m now zeroing in on the environmental constraints. I need to make sure the development server utilizes port 3000 and bypass `window.alert` and `window.open` calls. I\'m also ensuring the `metadata.json` file is correctly handled regarding name and description on the initial setup, ensuring permissions and capabilities, especially the `MAJOR_CAPABILITY` are maintained.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Intent**\n\nI\'m now very focused on understanding the user\'s explicit intent. The prompt \"install n8n\" is the only thing driving my current thought process. I\'m taking the instruction: \"Unless the user explicitly requests an AI feature, do not add chatbots, assistants, or LLM API calls\" very seriously. Therefore, I need to focus on what the user truly wants when asking to \"install n8n\" without presuming an AI assistant! They most likely expect the n8n Workflow Automation Platform & Studio with its interactive visual interface, which I am now modeling directly from n8n\'s UI with the signature elements.\n\n\n**Defining Core Execution Nodes**\n\nI\'m now detailing the core execution nodes required. The focus is on implementing essential functionalities mirroring n8n\'s features. This includes: Webhook triggers, scheduled triggers, manual triggers and HTTP requests. I\'m also implementing the Code Node with JavaScript sandbox support, the Edit Fields (Set Node) functionality for data transformation, conditional branching via the If / Condition Node, notification capabilities for emails and webhooks, and the JSON Parse/Transform node for data manipulation. Compatibility with n8n JSON imports and exports is also a key component.\n\n\n**Detailing Deployment Features**\n\nI\'m now detailing deployment features for a smooth n8n setup. A key focus is on ensuring the visual workflow generates compatible JSON for direct import into production n8n instances. I\'m also including a pre-loaded interactive template library to assist with common workflows. I\'m designing real execution tracing, showing input and output data for each node, and an execution history log for debugging. For users requesting an install, I\'m integrating an interactive \"Self-Host / Install n8n\" section with a Docker Compose generator.\n\n\n"
