  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Workflow Architecture**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing the architecture for the n8n Workflow Studio & Installation Hub. I\'m starting to map out the file structure, specifically thinking about the TypeScript code. I\'ve begun to define `src/types/workflow.ts` and am considering various `NodeType` options, including a `webhook` trigger node, incorporating both simulated and live webhook functionalities.\n\n\n**Expanding Node Types**\n\nI\'m expanding the types for nodes within the workflow. I am defining detailed specifications, covering aspects like URL, HTTP methods, and payloads. I\'m introducing key node types like `schedule` (trigger based on interval/cron), `manual`, `httpRequest`, and `code` for custom JavaScript execution. Other considerations are `editFields`, `if`, `filter`, `slackWebhook`, and `email` for specific workflow functionalities. I am defining WorkflowNode details.\n\n\n**Implementing Interoperability Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating n8n\'s JSON format into the workflow application. My current focus is the `n8nJsonConverter.ts` file, where I\'m implementing bidirectional conversion. This will allow for the seamless import of external n8n workflows and exporting workflows from the canvas, ensuring complete compatibility. I am leveraging standard n8n node types, like `webhook`, `httpRequest`, and `code`.\n\n\n**Defining Node Data Flow**\n\nNow, I\'m defining how data flows between the various node types. Specifically, I am refining the payload passing, trigger metadata for scheduled tasks, and the fetch function integration into the httpRequest node. I\'m also ensuring that the code node executes custom JavaScript and returns data correctly formatted, including error handling. Detailed output data and execution timing will be tracked node-by-node.\n\n\n**Designing Installation Hub**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the Installation Hub in `src/components/InstallHub.tsx`. I\'m designing a Docker Compose generator with options for PostgreSQL or SQLite, custom domain/webhook URLs, ports, and timezone settings. I\'m including an encryption key generator and one-click copy features for deployment commands. I\'m also preparing a quickstart guide for npm installations, including common troubleshooting tips and 1-click cloud deployments for Railway and Render.\n\n\n**Expanding Deployment Options**\n\nI\'m expanding the Installation Hub, now targeting cloud deployments like DigitalOcean 1-Click, Google Cloud Run, Elestio, and AWS Lightsail, providing direct links and deploy button instructions. I\'m also including tutorials for ngrok and Cloudflare Tunnel configurations to help with webhook delivery. Furthermore, a remote instance pinger is being designed, allowing users to test their n8n instance or webhook URLs.\n\n**Developing Workflow Canvas**\n\nMy focus has shifted to the `WorkflowCanvas.tsx` component. I am developing an interactive SVG canvas with pan/zoom functionality, draggable nodes with smooth physics, and Bezier connecting curves with animated pulses to represent data flow. I am incorporating output and input connection handles, drag-to-connect functionality, node selection features (including an orange n8n ring), and status badges. I\'m also implementing the ability to delete connections and nodes, duplicate nodes, and add nodes via a floating quick bar. Finally, I will be working on `NodeInspector.tsx`.\n\n\n**Refining Node Inspector**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `NodeInspector.tsx` component, the most recent update. I\'m building out a tabbed interface with Parameter, Input Data, Output Data, and Execution History views. I\'m focusing on the \"Send Webhook to Workflow\" button\'s design, which provides a simulator for live webhook testing. The node library has a categorized palette for nodes now, in the NodeLibraryModal.tsx.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_490515"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export type NodeType =\\n  | \'webhook\'\\n  | \'schedule\'\\n  | \'manual\'\\n  | \'httpRequest\'\\n  | \'code\'\\n  | \'editFields\'\\n  | \'if\'\\n  | \'filter\'\\n  | \'slackWebhook\'\\n  | \'email\';\\n\\nexport interface NodeCategory {\\n  id: \'trigger\' | \'action\' | \'transform\' | \'flow\';\\n  label: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface NodeDefinition {\\n  type: NodeType;\\n  name: string;\\n  category: \'trigger\' | \'action\' | \'transform\' | \'flow\';\\n  icon: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  defaultParameters: Record<string, any>;\\n  inputs: number;\\n  outputs: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface WorkflowNode {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  type: NodeType;\\n  position: [number, number];\\n  parameters: Record<string, any>;\\n  status?: \'idle\' | \'running\' | \'success\' | \'error\';\\n  executionResult?: {\\n    input?: any;\\n    output?: any;\\n    durationMs?: number;\\n    error?: string;\\n    timestamp?: string;\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport interface WorkflowConnection {\\n  id: string;\\n  fromNodeId: string;\\n  fromOutputIndex: number;\\n  toNodeId: string;\\n  toInputIndex: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface Workflow {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  active: boolean;\\n  nodes: WorkflowNode[];\\n  connections: WorkflowConnection[];\\n  updatedAt: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface ExecutionLogEntry {\\n  id: string;\\n  workflowId: string;\\n  workflowName: string;\\n  status: \'success\' | \'error\' | \'running\';\\n  startedAt: string;\\n  durationMs: number;\\n  triggeredBy: string;\\n  nodeCount: number;\\n  itemCount: number;\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Define types for n8n workflows, nodes, connections, and execution results\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/types/workflow.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating workflow types\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create workflow types\"}"
