    response: "### n8n Workflow Studio & Self-Hosting Hub\n\nThe application has been configured with an **n8n Workflow Automation Studio** and an interactive **Self-Hosting & Deployment Hub**:\n\n#### 1. Self-Hosting & Installation Hub\n* **Docker & Docker Compose Generator**: Configure database engines (PostgreSQL or SQLite), custom host ports (`5678`), webhook domains, timezone, and generate 32-character encryption keys with copyable `docker-compose.yml` and instant `docker run` one-liners.\n* **npm CLI Quickstart**: Step-by-step commands (`npm install -g n8n`, `n8n start`) with troubleshooting for permission errors and Node.js LTS versions.\n* **1-Click Cloud Deployments**: Direct deployment guides for Railway, Render, DigitalOcean 1-Click Droplet, and n8n Cloud.\n* **Webhook Tunnels**: Tunnel configurations using `n8n start --tunnel` or Cloudflare Tunnel to receive webhooks locally.\n* **Live Instance Connector**: Direct connection test to probe any running n8n instance and dispatch test webhook payloads.\n\n#### 2. Interactive Visual Workflow Canvas\n* **Full Node Graph Builder**: Draggable nodes, SVG Bezier connecting wires, animated execution pulses, input/output port handles, and zoom/pan controls.\n* **Supported Nodes**:\n  * **Triggers**: Webhook, Schedule (Cron/Interval), Manual Test Run\n  * **Actions & Transforms**: HTTP Request (REST API fetch), Code (JavaScript `$input.all()`), Edit Fields (Set), If (Conditional branching), Filter, Slack/Discord Webhooks, Email Notifications\n* **Node Inspector**: Configure parameters, view incoming data (`$input.item.json`), toggle between Table and JSON output views, and execute isolated single-step tests.\n* **Real Workflow Execution Engine**: Topologically executes connected pipelines with live node status badges and latency metrics.\n\n#### 3. n8n Compatibility & Webhook Simulator\n* **Export & Import n8n JSON**: Generates standard n8n workflow JSON ready to paste or upload directly into any official n8n instance, or import existing n8n workflows into the canvas.\n* **Webhook Simulator**: Test trigger workflows with Stripe, GitHub, or Shopify payloads or custom JSON, with cURL generation."
    thinking: "**Confirming TypeScript Success**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the TypeScript check and build concluded without any errors! Now, I\'m shifting my focus to the frontend design guidelines. Specifically, I\'m reviewing the checklist from `frontend-design`. The top bar contract dictates three zones, precisely separated by a gap of eight. I\'m taking this guideline into account.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### n8n Workflow Studio & Self-Hosting Hub\n\nThe application has been configured with an **n8n Workflow Automation Studio** and an interactive **Self-Hosting & Deployment Hub**:\n\n#### 1. Self-Hosting & Installation Hub\n* **Docker & Docker Compose Generator**: Configure database engines (PostgreSQL or SQLite), custom host ports (`5678`), webhook domains, timezone, and generate 32-character encryption keys with copyable `docker-compose.yml` and instant `docker run` one-liners.\n* **npm CLI Quickstart**: Step-by-step commands (`npm install -g n8n`, `n8n start`) with troubleshooting for permission errors and Node.js LTS versions.\n* **1-Click Cloud Deployments**: Direct deployment guides for Railway, Render, DigitalOcean 1-Click Droplet, and n8n Cloud.\n* **Webhook Tunnels**: Tunnel configurations using `n8n start --tunnel` or Cloudflare Tunnel to receive webhooks locally.\n* **Live Instance Connector**: Direct connection test to probe any running n8n instance and dispatch test webhook payloads.\n\n#### 2. Interactive Visual Workflow Canvas\n* **Full Node Graph Builder**: Draggable nodes, SVG Bezier connecting wires, animated execution pulses, input/output port handles, and zoom/pan controls.\n* **Supported Nodes**:\n  * **Triggers**: Webhook, Schedule (Cron/Interval), Manual Test Run\n  * **Actions & Transforms**: HTTP Request (REST API fetch), Code (JavaScript `$input.all()`), Edit Fields (Set), If (Conditional branching), Filter, Slack/Discord Webhooks, Email Notifications\n* **Node Inspector**: Configure parameters, view incoming data (`$input.item.json`), toggle between Table and JSON output views, and execute isolated single-step tests.\n* **Real Workflow Execution Engine**: Topologically executes connected pipelines with live node status badges and latency metrics.\n\n#### 3. n8n Compatibility & Webhook Simulator\n* **Export & Import n8n JSON**: Generates standard n8n workflow JSON ready to paste or upload directly into any official n8n instance, or import existing n8n workflows into the canvas.\n* **Webhook Simulator**: Test trigger workflows with Stripe, GitHub, or Shopify payloads or custom JSON, with cURL generation."
