  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Developer Integrations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on creating a `DeveloperIntegrationsView` component. My goal is to showcase the top 5 n8n integrations most beneficial to developers. I\'ve started identifying key examples, such as the GitHub integration, and outlining its developer-centric applications, like CI/CD webhooks and automated PR workflows. I\'m aiming to provide a compelling, actionable list.\n\n\n**Expanding Integration Scenarios**\n\nI\'m now diving into specific use-cases beyond GitHub, exploring how n8n can address complex developer workflows. I\'ve detailed PostgreSQL applications, from event-driven database mutations to automated backups and health checks. I\'m also outlining workflows for the HTTP Request Node, highlighting its versatility with microservices and third-party APIs. Finally, the integration with Slack/Discord is becoming clearer in my mind.\n\n\n**Detailing New Integration Examples**\n\nI\'m now outlining a DeveloperOps Bot use case, exploring interactive ChatOps with deployment approvals and incident response triage, triggered from alerts. I\'m also examining the automation possibilities with AWS S3, including asset pipelines and user document processing, as well as a starter workflow for form-to-CRM contact synchronization. I\'ve broken down each use case into detailed workflows, which I\'m presenting alongside \"Load into Editor\" options. I\'m thinking about how to integrate all of this into `src/components/DeveloperIntegrationsView.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_345479"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import React from \'react\';\\nimport {\\n  GitPullRequest,\\n  Database,\\n  Globe,\\n  MessageSquare,\\n  HardDrive,\\n  ArrowRight,\\n  CheckCircle2,\\n  Play,\\n  Layers,\\n  Code2,\\n  Users\\n} from \'lucide-react\';\\nimport { WORKFLOW_TEMPLATES } from \'../data/templates\';\\nimport { Workflow } from \'../types/workflow\';\\n\\ninterface DeveloperIntegrationsViewProps {\\n  onLoadWorkflow: (workflow: Workflow) => void;\\n  onGoToCanvas: () => void;\\n}\\n\\nexport const DeveloperIntegrationsView: React.FC<DeveloperIntegrationsViewProps> = ({\\n  onLoadWorkflow,\\n  onGoToCanvas,\\n}) => {\\n  const crmTemplate = WORKFLOW_TEMPLATES.find(t => t.id === \'tpl-form-crm-sync\') || WORKFLOW_TEMPLATES[0];\\n  const githubTemplate = WORKFLOW_TEMPLATES.find(t => t.id === \'tpl-github-devops\') || WORKFLOW_TEMPLATES[1];\\n\\n  const TOP_INTEGRATIONS = [\\n    {\\n      id: \'github\',\\n      title: \'1. GitHub & Gitlab Integration\',\\n      badge: \'DevOps & CI/CD\',\\n      icon: GitPullRequest,\\n      accent: \'text-purple-400\',\\n      description:\\n        \'Listen to repository webhooks (PR opened, review submitted, release published, branch merged) and automate CI/CD triggers, linear/Jira ticket synchronization, and team alerts.\',\\n      workflowSummary: \'GitHub Webhook (PR Closed) \342\206\222 Code Status Evaluator \342\206\222 IF Merged to Main \342\206\222 Slack Ops Channel Notification\',\\n      template: githubTemplate,\\n      benefits: [\\n        \'Automate PR triage and auto-assign engineering reviewers based on touched filepaths\',\\n        \'Auto-generate release notes from closed PRs and push to Confluence or Slack\',\\n        \'Synchronize bug issues between GitHub and project trackers (Linear, Jira)\',\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    {\\n      id: \'postgres\',\\n      title: \'2. PostgreSQL & Relational DBs\',\\n      badge: \'Data & State Management\',\\n      icon: Database,\\n      accent: \'text-sky-400\',\\n      description:\\n        \'Execute parameterized SQL queries, listen to LISTEN/NOTIFY events, perform bulk ETL migrations, and safely mutate records across transactional databases.\',\\n      workflowSummary: \'Schedule Cron (Every 15m) \342\206\222 Execute SQL Query (Pending Orders) \342\206\222 Transform to JSON Array \342\206\222 Bulk Upsert Target\',\\n      template: WORKFLOW_TEMPLATES.find(t => t.id === \'tpl-data-etl\') || WORKFLOW_TEMPLATES[0],\\n      benefits: [\\n        \'Event-driven database mutations without custom cron daemon infrastructure\',\\n        \'Extract, transform, and load (ETL) data pipelines into analytics data warehouses\',\\n        \'Automated database health audits, slow query logging, and table archival\',\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    {\\n      id: \'http\',\\n      title: \'3. HTTP Request Node (Universal REST / GraphQL / gRPC)\',\\n      badge: \'Universal API Bridge\',\\n      icon: Globe,\\n      accent: \'text-emerald-400\',\\n      description:\\n        \'The developer swiss-army knife in n8n. Connect to any internal microservice, proprietary VPC endpoint, or external API with full control over headers, query parameters, Bearer tokens, and multipart payloads.\',\\n      workflowSummary: \'Inbound Webhook \342\206\222 Inject Authorization Headers \342\206\222 Fetch / Mutate Remote API \342\206\222 Map Response JSON\',\\n      template: WORKFLOW_TEMPLATES.find(t => t.id === \'tpl-api-monitor\') || WORKFLOW_TEMPLATES[0],\\n      benefits: [\\n        \'Call any internal REST or GraphQL microservice without waiting for a prebuilt plugin\',\\n        \'Built-in pagination handling, automatic retry with exponential backoff\',\\n        \'Transform external API payloads before forwarding to downstream listeners\',\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    {\\n      id: \'slack\',\\n      title: \'4. Slack / Discord (ChatOps & Interactive Approvals)\',\\n      badge: \'ChatOps & Incident Response\',\\n      icon: MessageSquare,\\n      accent: \'text-[#ff6d5a]\',\\n      description:\\n        \'Turn Slack and Discord into a complete ChatOps command center. Post formatted rich block alerts, receive slash commands, and implement two-way approval buttons (e.g. human-in-the-loop deployment gating).\',\\n      workflowSummary: \'Sentry / Alertmanager Webhook \342\206\222 Severity Check \342\206\222 Interactive Slack Card with \\\"Acknowledge\\\" & \\\"Restart Service\\\" Buttons\',\\n      template: WORKFLOW_TEMPLATES.find(t => t.id === \'tpl-webhook-slack\') || WORKFLOW_TEMPLATES[0],\\n      benefits: [\\n        \'Interactive approval workflows where engineers click buttons inside Slack to approve staging deploys\',\\n        \'Route error stack traces from Sentry/Datadog to on-call developers with direct links\',\\n        \'Slash commands that trigger internal administrative runbooks and database resets\',\\n      ],\\n    },\\n    {\\n      id: \'s3\',\\n      title: \'5. AWS S3 / Cloudflare R2 / Cloud Storage\',\\n      badge: \'File & Asset Pipelines\',\\n      icon: HardDrive,\\n      accent: \'text-amber-400\',\\n      description:\\n        \'Automate binary file uploads, document transformation, scheduled database dump storage, and programmatic generation of pre-signed URLs for clients.\',\\n      workflowSummary: \'Form File Attachment Upload \342\206\222 S3 PutObject \342\206\222 Extract Document Metadata \342\206\222 Store Storage Key in CRM / DB\',\\n      template: crmTemplate,\\n      benefits: [\\n        \'Ingest user-uploaded files, generate thumbnails/transcripts, and save directly to object buckets\',\\n        \'Nightly backup pipelines that pull DB snapshots and upload encrypted archives to cold storage\',\\n        \'Sync assets between cloud providers (e.g. S3 to Cloudflare R2 for zero-egress distribution)\',\\n      ],\\n    },\\n  ];\\n\\n  return (\\n    <div className=\\\"max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 space-y-10\\\">\\n      {/* Hero: Form to CRM Featured Starter Workflow */}\\n      <div className=\\\"border border-[#ff6d5a]/40 bg-gradient-to-r from-slate-900 via-slate-900 to-slate-950 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-xl shadow-xl space-y-6\\\">\\n        <div className=\\\"flex flex-col md:flex-row items-start md:items-center justify-between gap-4\\\">\\n          <div className=\\\"space-y-1.5\\\">\\n            <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-[#ff6d5a]\\\">\\n              <span>RECOMMENDED STARTER WORKFLOW</span>\\n              <span>\302\267</span>\\n              <span>CRM INTEGRATION</span>\\n            </div>\\n            <h2 className=\\\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white flex items-center gap-2\\\">\\n              <Users className=\\\"w-6 h-6 text-[#ff6d5a]\\\" />\\n              Sync New Contacts from Form to CRM\\n            </h2>\\n            <p className=\\\"text-sm text-slate-300 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed\\\">\\n              A standard, production-ready pipeline that receives incoming lead submissions, cleans and validates\\n              contact data via JavaScript, checks for existing records in your CRM via REST API, upserts the contact,\\n              and notifies the sales team.\\n            </p>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          <button\\n            onClick={() => {\\n              onLoadWorkflow(crmTemplate);\\n              onGoToCanvas();\\n            }}\\n            className=\\\"px-5 py-2.5 bg-[#ff6d5a] hover:bg-[#ea503c] text-white font-semibold text-xs rounded-lg transition-colors shadow-lg shadow-[#ff6d5a]/20 flex items-center gap-2 shrink-0\\\"\\n          >\\n            <Play className=\\\"w-4 h-4 fill-current\\\" />\\n            <span>Load &amp; Run Starter Workflow</span>\\n          </button>\\n        </div>\\n\\n        {/* Visual Pipeline Steps */}\\n        <div className=\\\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-3 pt-2\\\">\\n          <div className=\\\"bg-slate-950 p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 space-y-1.5\\\">\\n            <span className=\\\"text-[10px] font-mono text-slate-500 uppercase\\\">Step 1 \302\267 Trigger</span>\\n            <div className=\\\"text-xs font-semibold text-white\\\">Form Webhook</div>\\n            <p className=\\\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\\\">Captures name, email, company, and phone</p>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          <div className=\\\"bg-slate-950 p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 space-y-1.5\\\">\\n            <span className=\\\"text-[10px] font-mono text-slate-500 uppercase\\\">Step 2 \302\267 Transform</span>\\n            <div className=\\\"text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-400\\\">Code Normalizer</div>\\n            <p className=\\\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\\\">Trims email, calculates lead score, formats phone</p>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          <div className=\\\"bg-slate-950 p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 space-y-1.5\\\">\\n            <span className=\\\"text-[10px] font-mono text-slate-500 uppercase\\\">Step 3 \302\267 Query</span>\\n            <div className=\\\"text-xs font-semibold text-sky-400\\\">CRM GET Request</div>\\n            <p className=\\\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\\\">Queries CRM (HubSpot/Salesforce/Postgres) by email</p>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          <div className=\\\"bg-slate-950 p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 space-y-1.5\\\">\\n            <span className=\\\"text-[10px] font-mono text-slate-500 uppercase\\\">Step 4 \302\267 Logic</span>\\n            <div className=\\\"text-xs font-semibold text-amber-400\\\">IF Condition</div>\\n            <p className=\\\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\\\">Routes to Create New Lead or Update Existing</p>\\n          </div>\\n\\n          <div className=\\\"bg-slate-950 p-3.5 rounded-lg border border-slate-800 space-y-1.5\\\">\\n            <span className=\\\"text-[10px] font-mono text-slate-500 uppercase\\\">Step 5 \302\267 Alert</span>\\n            <div className=\\\"text-xs font-semibold text-[#ff6d5a]\\\">Slack Notification</div>\\n            <p className=\\\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\\\">Dispatches real-time lead alert to sales channel</p>\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n      </div>\\n\\n      {/* Top 5 Developer Integrations */}\\n      <div className=\\\"space-y-6\\\">\\n        <div>\\n          <h3 className=\\\"text-xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight\\\">\\n            Top 5 Most Useful n8n Integrations for Developers\\n          </h3>\\n          <p className=\\\"text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1\\\">\\n            Engineered for automation of software lifecycles, databases, microservices, and incident response.\\n          </p>\\n        </div>\\n\\n        <div className=\\\"space-y-4\\\">\\n          {TOP_INTEGRATIONS.map(item => {\\n            const Icon = item.icon;\\n            return (\\n              <div\\n                key={item.id}\\n                className=\\\"border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 p-6 rounded-xl space-y-4 hover:border-slate-700 transition-colors\\\"\\n              >\\n                <div className=\\\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-3\\\">\\n                  <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-3\\\">\\n                    <div className=\\\"w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 flex items-center justify-center shrink-0\\\">\\n                      <Icon className={`w-5 h-5 ${item.accent}`} />\\n                    </div>\\n                    <div>\\n                      <h4 className=\\\"text-base font-semibold text-white\\\">{item.title}</h4>\\n                      <span className=\\\"text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-400\\\">{item.badge}</span>\\n                    </div>\\n                  </div>\\n\\n                  <button\\n                    onClick={() => {\\n                      onLoadWorkflow(item.template);\\n                      onGoToCanvas();\\n                    }}\\n                    className=\\\"px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-200 hover:text-white text-xs font-medium rounded-lg transition-colors flex items-center gap-1.5 shrink-0\\\"\\n                  >\\n                    <span>Load Template into Canvas</span>\\n                    <ArrowRight className=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5\\\" />\\n                  </button>\\n                </div>\\n\\n                <p className=\\\"text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed\\\">{item.description}</p>\\n\\n                {/* Workflow Sequence */}\\n                <div className=\\\"bg-slate-950 p-3 rounded-lg border border-slate-800/80 space-y-1\\\">\\n                  <span className=\\\"text-[10px] font-mono text-slate-500 uppercase\\\">\\n                    Example Workflow Architecture:\\n                  </span>\\n                  <div className=\\\"text-xs font-mono text-emerald-400\\\">{item.workflowSummary}</div>\\n                </div>\\n\\n                {/* Use cases */}\\n                <div className=\\\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-2.5 pt-1\\\">\\n                  {item.benefits.map((benefit, i) => (\\n                    <div key={i} className=\\\"flex items-start gap-2 text-xs text-slate-400\\\">\\n                      <CheckCircle2 className=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5 text-slate-500 shrink-0 mt-0.5\\\" />\\n                      <span>{benefit}</span>\\n                    </div>\\n                  ))}\\n                </div>\\n              </div>\\n            );\\n          })}\\n        </div>\\n      </div>\\n    </div>\\n  );\\n};\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create DeveloperIntegrationsView component explaining top 5 integrations and starter CRM workflow\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/DeveloperIntegrationsView.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating DeveloperIntegrationsView component\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create DeveloperIntegrationsView\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\321\026\n\316\026\001i\024}\023O\037\3309x\001k>U\226\006\305:\026\256z\003\321\002\376\3014\016,\367\353:\021\f:\260\3038\\\2075Xp\212\314\247!o_\037\337I`\345\224\334/\267\340:\256<\271u\325H\254p?{\006\227\265\303D\022\253_K\'\327\020\200=\310\035w\231\327\274\2313\201\361>\366\277\200\367\252\020t\004\321\357\312Lr\213\364V\320\363\344\352\222\360F\336^ \372\237qK\333\v\310fUvH\025T\215\362\206\035\243T\301J9\275{G)\016:\265\231Eo\024\352\034\311\363a<8\336tZ\311\017\340P\032\262G\320\2771\273\247\215?\241\016g\n-[\016\f%|\304\365zK\273\257d\004\221?\364/\177\016\024\270Z\b\255\210\037\274-s\325\026\262\v\306\177T\311\005\217\210C%\215\n>N\020\353\\\212\206C\300\005\242$\0364\177-\352\270\316\3405\216\023m\037\231\327\363(\b\366\b\313\360\241\247\0306\364~\352\230\313\233\246\363VbW[\331\200\024\006\3030t~/gl\245\231\333\267\036\2365w\202\230\342\320vBP\211 l\016\225\240\313^\001C\240{\323\216D\200\203V\322\'\235\323\315\272qs4\033\336\207\243\306\026C\354]\324\321\332>P\021l\323\225\270\216\213r\211tbA\354(\350\221\3332V\225\2742f)W\177\204\202\200\355hg\254/|\360oe\324\363\000r\357&\240\365\241\227\362\305\217\315\0161<e~+]\316\202\']\006y#QHU9u\315b\277\v\230\027\271\003\210\230\340\271=\325\202\201\033\303\357\204\024\036U\b\315\020s\034\317U4\365\n_\213\253\v_\203x{ec\3554m\346\207\271\333t\341\3406\347A\"\240*(R\031\220\317\377\370\\\200\337\\\345\376C\250\370\210\327\ba\336\2341u)\247\003I\215OE\021\274 \247U\204d\006\337\343\b\350,\227h\'\344{N\275\276\261\345\265Csf\"\247\226\255\215\342\031|%;\246\303\030EE\312\272\374O\324[3\035\336\255\233X\346^\312\2119\341\327\031\212J\256\353#Z\303\323\221\336a]k\312\333\203\200\003^z<\353i\311U_=\371\334nPL\347\'\332\317C\"\232l\246D\273\037\0307\263v\221,YL\020\335\203\016s\334\307y\344\250d\003\300d-\277%X\\W\362\302\234\344W\227\306\027b\177\236\225\204\207\255\331\r\255_%\341\331<\264V\347\375\346*\036\033O\276\2159+\371\331d\335\255m\251\223\325\030\222t\356\025x\035\352\322\2