  }
  planner_response {
    response: "### Top 5 Most Useful n8n Integrations for Developers\n\nHere are the five most impactful integrations in n8n for software engineers and dev teams:\n\n---\n\n#### 1. GitHub / GitLab (DevOps & CI/CD Automation)\n* **How to Leverage It**: Listen to repository webhooks (`pull_request`, `push`, `release`, `issues`) to automate engineering tasks without writing custom GitHub Action bots. Automatically label issues, notify Slack channels when hotfixes are merged, generate release notes, and sync PR reviews with issue tracking (e.g., Linear, Jira).\n* **Example Workflow**:\n  $$\\text{GitHub Webhook (PR Closed)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Code (Filter for Merged to Main)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{HTTP Request (Trigger Cloud Run / CI Build)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Slack Bot (Post release summary)}$$\n\n---\n\n#### 2. PostgreSQL & Relational Databases (Data Sync & State Pipelines)\n* **How to Leverage It**: Execute parameterized SQL queries, listen to `LISTEN/NOTIFY` channels, and schedule transactional ETL pipelines without managing crontab daemons. Clean and move data between production and analytics warehouses (BigQuery, Snowflake), and reprocess dead-letter queues.\n* **Example Workflow**:\n  $$\\text{Schedule Trigger (Every 15 min)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Postgres Node (SELECT * WHERE status=\'pending\')} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Code (Normalize JSON)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Postgres Node (UPDATE status=\'processed\')}$$\n\n---\n\n#### 3. HTTP Request Node (Universal REST / GraphQL / Microservice Bridge)\n* **How to Leverage It**: The universal developer tool in n8n. Connects to any internal microservice, private VPC endpoint, or 3rd-party API with custom headers, OAuth2/Bearer tokens, query parameters, multipart form uploads, and built-in pagination handling with automatic retries.\n* **Example Workflow**:\n  $$\\text{Inbound Webhook} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Code (Prepare JWT / Payload)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{HTTP Request (POST to internal auth service)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{If (Status == 200)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Forward downstream}$$\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Slack & Discord (ChatOps & Interactive Deployment Approvals)\n* **How to Leverage It**: Turn chat channels into a complete ChatOps command console. Post rich Block Kit cards with interactive buttons (e.g., \"Approve Staging Deploy\", \"Restart Pod\"), receive slash commands (`/db-reset`, `/user-lookup`), and dispatch error stack traces from Sentry/Datadog to on-call engineers.\n* **Example Workflow**:\n  $$\\text{Alertmanager / Sentry Webhook} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{If (Severity == \'critical\')} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Slack Node (Interactive Block with \"Acknowledge\" & \"Rollback\" buttons)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Wait for click}$$\n\n---\n\n#### 5. AWS S3 / Cloudflare R2 / Object Storage (Asset & Backup Pipelines)\n* **How to Leverage It**: Automate file ingestion, document archiving, night-time database backup uploads, and generation of pre-signed URLs. Integrates seamlessly with binary streams without needing local disk writes.\n* **Example Workflow**:\n  $$\\text{Form File Upload Webhook} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{S3 Node (Upload buffer to bucket)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Code (Extract file hash & generate CDN URL)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Update Database}$$\n\n---\n\n### Setting Up n8n on Your System\n\n#### Option A: Docker (Recommended for Reliability & Production)\n\n1. **Prerequisite**: Install Docker Desktop (or Docker Engine on Linux).\n2. **Run n8n in a single command**:\n   ```bash\n   docker run -d \\\n     --name n8n \\\n     -p 5678:5678 \\\n     -e N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY=\"replace_with_a_random_32_character_key\" \\\n     -e GENERIC_TIMEZONE=\"UTC\" \\\n     -v n8n_data:/home/node/.n8n \\\n     docker.n8n.io/n8nio/n8n\n   ```\n\n3. **Or run with Docker Compose (with PostgreSQL)**:\n   Create a `docker-compose.yml` file:\n   ```yaml\n   version: \'3.8\'\n\n   volumes:\n     n8n_data:\n     postgres_data:\n\n   services:\n     postgres:\n       image: postgres:16-alpine\n       container_name: n8n-postgres\n       restart: unless-stopped\n       environment:\n         - POSTGRES_USER=n8n\n         - POSTGRES_PASSWORD=n8n_secure_db_pass\n         - POSTGRES_DB=n8n\n       volumes:\n         - postgres_data:/var/lib/postgresql/data\n       healthcheck:\n         test: [\'CMD-SHELL\', \'pg_isready -h localhost -U n8n -d n8n\']\n         interval: 5s\n         timeout: 5s\n         retries: 10\n\n     n8n:\n       image: docker.n8n.io/n8nio/n8n:latest\n       container_name: n8n-server\n       restart: unless-stopped\n       ports:\n         - \"5678:5678\"\n       environment:\n         - DB_TYPE=postgresdb\n         - DB_POSTGRESDB_HOST=postgres\n         - DB_POSTGRESDB_PORT=5432\n         - DB_POSTGRESDB_DATABASE=n8n\n         - DB_POSTGRESDB_USER=n8n\n         - DB_POSTGRESDB_PASSWORD=n8n_secure_db_pass\n         - N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace_with_a_random_32_character_key\n         - GENERIC_TIMEZONE=UTC\n         - EXECUTIONS_DATA_PRUNE=true\n       volumes:\n         - n8n_data:/home/node/.n8n\n       depends_on:\n         postgres:\n           condition: service_healthy\n   ```\n   Start the stack:\n   ```bash\n   docker compose up -d\n   ```\n\n---\n\n#### Option B: npm Global Install (Fast Local Node.js Setup)\n\nIf you have **Node.js LTS (v18, v20, or v22)** and npm installed:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Install n8n globally\nnpm install -g n8n\n\n# 2. Start n8n\nn8n start\n```\n\n*Note: If you run into permission errors on Linux/macOS, configure npm to use a user-owned directory (`mkdir ~/.npm-global && npm config set prefix \'~/.npm-global\'`) rather than using `sudo`.*\n\n---\n\n### Initial Configuration Checklist\n\n1. **Access the Editor**: Open `http://localhost:5678` in your browser.\n2. **Create Owner Account**: On first launch, n8n prompts you to create the initial admin user (email and password).\n3. **Webhook URL**: If your workflows need to receive webhooks from third-party services (like Stripe, GitHub, or Typeform) while running locally, launch n8n with `--tunnel` or use Cloudflare Tunnel:\n   ```bash\n   n8n start --tunnel\n   # OR\n   cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:5678\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### Starter Workflow: Syncing New Contacts from a Form to a CRM\n\nThis exact starter workflow is pre-loaded into your **n8n Workflow Studio** applet.\n\n#### Workflow Node Sequence:\n1. **Webhook Trigger (Form Submission)**:\n   * **Endpoint**: `POST /webhook/lead-form`\n   * **Payload**:\n     ```json\n     {\n       \"firstName\": \"Maya\",\n       \"lastName\": \"Lin\",\n       \"email\": \"maya.lin@innovatech.io\",\n       \"company\": \"InnovaTech Cloud\",\n       \"jobTitle\": \"VP of Engineering\",\n       \"phone\": \"+1 (555) 382-9012\"\n     }\n     ```\n2. **Code Node (Data Sanitization & Scoring)**:\n   * Trims whitespace, lowercases the email, formats the contact name, and assigns a preliminary lead score:\n     ```javascript\n     const items = $input.all();\n     return items.map(item => {\n       const data = item.json || item;\n       const cleanEmail = (data.email || \'\').trim().toLowerCase();\n       const fullName = [data.firstName, data.lastName].filter(Boolean).join(\' \').trim();\n       return {\n         json: {\n           ...data,\n           fullName,\n           email: cleanEmail,\n           leadScore: (data.jobTitle || \'\').toLowerCase().includes(\'vp\') ? 85 : 50,\n           syncedAt: new Date().toISOString()\n         }\n       };\n     });\n     ```\n3. **HTTP Request Node (Search CRM)**:\n   * Calls your CRM API (HubSpot, Salesforce, Pipedrive, or custom DB): `GET /api/v1/contacts?email={{$json.email}}`.\n4. **IF Condition Node**:\n   * Condition: Check if record exists (`id` is not empty).\n   * **True Branch**: Call `PUT /api/v1/contacts/{{$json.id}}` to update existing contact.\n   * **False Branch**: Call `POST /api/v1/contacts` to create a new lead.\n5. **Slack / Email Notification**:\n   * Dispatches an alert to your `#sales-leads` channel with the lead details and lead score.\n\n---\n\n### Live Studio Features Now Available in Your App\n\n* **Interactive Developer Integrations View**: Inspect and 1-click load all 5 developer workflows and the Form-to-CRM sync into the canvas.\n* **Visual Canvas**: Drag and drop nodes, test individual steps, and run topological workflow executions.\n* **Webhook Simulator**: Test the Form-to-CRM pipeline with sample Stripe, GitHub, or form payloads with real-time execution tracing.\n* **n8n JSON Export**: Download or copy standard n8n JSON from the canvas and paste it directly into your local or cloud n8n instance."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Integration Usefulness**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that both the compilation and linting processes have been completed successfully without any errors. My next focus will be constructing a detailed and reliable answer, which will address the user\'s specific requests. I\'ll outline the top 5 most practical n8n integrations for developers. These include: GitHub/GitLab, PostgreSQL/Relational Databases, HTTP Request node, Slack/Discord ChatOps, and AWS S3.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Top 5 Most Useful n8n Integrations for Developers\n\nHere are the five most impactful integrations in n8n for software engineers and dev teams:\n\n---\n\n#### 1. GitHub / GitLab (DevOps & CI/CD Automation)\n* **How to Leverage It**: Listen to repository webhooks (`pull_request`, `push`, `release`, `issues`) to automate engineering tasks without writing custom GitHub Action bots. Automatically label issues, notify Slack channels when hotfixes are merged, generate release notes, and sync PR reviews with issue tracking (e.g., Linear, Jira).\n* **Example Workflow**:\n  $$\\text{GitHub Webhook (PR Closed)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Code (Filter for Merged to Main)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{HTTP Request (Trigger Cloud Run / CI Build)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Slack Bot (Post release summary)}$$\n\n---\n\n#### 2. PostgreSQL & Relational Databases (Data Sync & State Pipelines)\n* **How to Leverage It**: Execute parameterized SQL queries, listen to `LISTEN/NOTIFY` channels, and schedule transactional ETL pipelines without managing crontab daemons. Clean and move data between production and analytics warehouses (BigQuery, Snowflake), and reprocess dead-letter queues.\n* **Example Workflow**:\n  $$\\text{Schedule Trigger (Every 15 min)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Postgres Node (SELECT * WHERE status=\'pending\')} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Code (Normalize JSON)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Postgres Node (UPDATE status=\'processed\')}$$\n\n---\n\n#### 3. HTTP Request Node (Universal REST / GraphQL / Microservice Bridge)\n* **How to Leverage It**: The universal developer tool in n8n. Connects to any internal microservice, private VPC endpoint, or 3rd-party API with custom headers, OAuth2/Bearer tokens, query parameters, multipart form uploads, and built-in pagination handling with automatic retries.\n* **Example Workflow**:\n  $$\\text{Inbound Webhook} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Code (Prepare JWT / Payload)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{HTTP Request (POST to internal auth service)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{If (Status == 200)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Forward downstream}$$\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Slack & Discord (ChatOps & Interactive Deployment Approvals)\n* **How to Leverage It**: Turn chat channels into a complete ChatOps command console. Post rich Block Kit cards with interactive buttons (e.g., \"Approve Staging Deploy\", \"Restart Pod\"), receive slash commands (`/db-reset`, `/user-lookup`), and dispatch error stack traces from Sentry/Datadog to on-call engineers.\n* **Example Workflow**:\n  $$\\text{Alertmanager / Sentry Webhook} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{If (Severity == \'critical\')} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Slack Node (Interactive Block with \"Acknowledge\" & \"Rollback\" buttons)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Wait for click}$$\n\n---\n\n#### 5. AWS S3 / Cloudflare R2 / Object Storage (Asset & Backup Pipelines)\n* **How to Leverage It**: Automate file ingestion, document archiving, night-time database backup uploads, and generation of pre-signed URLs. Integrates seamlessly with binary streams without needing local disk writes.\n* **Example Workflow**:\n  $$\\text{Form File Upload Webhook} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{S3 Node (Upload buffer to bucket)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Code (Extract file hash & generate CDN URL)} \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{Update Database}$$\n\n---\n\n### Setting Up n8n on Your System\n\n#### Option A: Docker (Recommended for Reliability & Production)\n\n1. **Prerequisite**: Install Docker Desktop (or Docker Engine on Linux).\n2. **Run n8n in a single command**:\n   ```bash\n   docker run -d \\\n     --name n8n \\\n     -p 5678:5678 \\\n     -e N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY=\"replace_with_a_random_32_character_key\" \\\n     -e GENERIC_TIMEZONE=\"UTC\" \\\n     -v n8n_data:/home/node/.n8n \\\n     docker.n8n.io/n8nio/n8n\n   ```\n\n3. **Or run with Docker Compose (with PostgreSQL)**:\n   Create a `docker-compose.yml` file:\n   ```yaml\n   version: \'3.8\'\n\n   volumes:\n     n8n_data:\n     postgres_data:\n\n   services:\n     postgres:\n       image: postgres:16-alpine\n       container_name: n8n-postgres\n       restart: unless-stopped\n       environment:\n         - POSTGRES_USER=n8n\n         - POSTGRES_PASSWORD=n8n_secure_db_pass\n         - POSTGRES_DB=n8n\n       volumes:\n         - postgres_data:/var/lib/postgresql/data\n       healthcheck:\n         test: [\'CMD-SHELL\', \'pg_isready -h localhost -U n8n -d n8n\']\n         interval: 5s\n         timeout: 5s\n         retries: 10\n\n     n8n:\n       image: docker.n8n.io/n8nio/n8n:latest\n       container_name: n8n-server\n       restart: unless-stopped\n       ports:\n         - \"5678:5678\"\n       environment:\n         - DB_TYPE=postgresdb\n         - DB_POSTGRESDB_HOST=postgres\n         - DB_POSTGRESDB_PORT=5432\n         - DB_POSTGRESDB_DATABASE=n8n\n         - DB_POSTGRESDB_USER=n8n\n         - DB_POSTGRESDB_PASSWORD=n8n_secure_db_pass\n         - N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace_with_a_random_32_character_key\n         - GENERIC_TIMEZONE=UTC\n         - EXECUTIONS_DATA_PRUNE=true\n       volumes:\n         - n8n_data:/home/node/.n8n\n       depends_on:\n         postgres:\n           condition: service_healthy\n   ```\n   Start the stack:\n   ```bash\n   docker compose up -d\n   ```\n\n---\n\n#### Option B: npm Global Install (Fast Local Node.js Setup)\n\nIf you have **Node.js LTS (v18, v20, or v22)** and npm installed:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Install n8n globally\nnpm install -g n8n\n\n# 2. Start n8n\nn8n start\n```\n\n*Note: If you run into permission errors on Linux/macOS, configure npm to use a user-owned directory (`mkdir ~/.npm-global && npm config set prefix \'~/.npm-global\'`) rather than using `sudo`.*\n\n---\n\n### Initial Configuration Checklist\n\n1. **Access the Editor**: Open `http://localhost:5678` in your browser.\n2. **Create Owner Account**: On first launch, n8n prompts you to create the initial admin user (email and password).\n3. **Webhook URL**: If your workflows need to receive webhooks from third-party services (like Stripe, GitHub, or Typeform) while running locally, launch n8n with `--tunnel` or use Cloudflare Tunnel:\n   ```bash\n   n8n start --tunnel\n   # OR\n   cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:5678\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### Starter Workflow: Syncing New Contacts from a Form to a CRM\n\nThis exact starter workflow is pre-loaded into your **n8n Workflow Studio** applet.\n\n#### Workflow Node Sequence:\n1. **Webhook Trigger (Form Submission)**:\n   * **Endpoint**: `POST /webhook/lead-form`\n   * **Payload**:\n     ```json\n     {\n       \"firstName\": \"Maya\",\n       \"lastName\": \"Lin\",\n       \"email\": \"maya.lin@innovatech.io\",\n       \"company\": \"InnovaTech Cloud\",\n       \"jobTitle\": \"VP of Engineering\",\n       \"phone\": \"+1 (555) 382-9012\"\n     }\n     ```\n2. **Code Node (Data Sanitization & Scoring)**:\n   * Trims whitespace, lowercases the email, formats the contact name, and assigns a preliminary lead score:\n     ```javascript\n     const items = $input.all();\n     return items.map(item => {\n       const data = item.json || item;\n       const cleanEmail = (data.email || \'\').trim().toLowerCase();\n       const fullName = [data.firstName, data.lastName].filter(Boolean).join(\' \').trim();\n       return {\n         json: {\n           ...data,\n           fullName,\n           email: cleanEmail,\n           leadScore: (data.jobTitle || \'\').toLowerCase().includes(\'vp\') ? 85 : 50,\n           syncedAt: new Date().toISOString()\n         }\n       };\n     });\n     ```\n3. **HTTP Request Node (Search CRM)**:\n   * Calls your CRM API (HubSpot, Salesforce, Pipedrive, or custom DB): `GET /api/v1/contacts?email={{$json.email}}`.\n4. **IF Condition Node**:\n   * Condition: Check if record exists (`id` is not empty).\n   * **True Branch**: Call `PUT /api/v1/contacts/{{$json.id}}` to update existing contact.\n   * **False Branch**: Call `POST /api/v1/contacts` to create a new lead.\n5. **Slack / Email Notification**:\n   * Dispatches an alert to your `#sales-leads` channel with the lead details and lead score.\n\n---\n\n### Live Studio Features Now Available in Your App\n\n* **Interactive Developer Integrations View**: Inspect and 1-click load all 5 developer workflows and the Form-to-CRM sync into the canvas.\n* **Visual Canvas**: Drag and drop nodes, test individual steps, and run topological workflow executions.\n* **Webhook Simulator**: Test the Form-to-CRM pipeline with sample Stripe, GitHub, or form payloads with real-time execution tracing.\n* **n8n JSON Export**: Download or copy standard n8n JSON from the canvas and paste it directly into your local or cloud n8n instance."
