  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Addressing MySQL Compatibility**\n\nI\'m focusing on ensuring compatibility with MySQL within the AI Studio container sandbox, even without a running daemon. I\'m exploring ways to handle schema migrations effectively, including the graceful detection of the MySQL server and the use of the `mysql2` connection pool. I\'m also considering auto-detecting/graceful fallback strategies, given the absence of the daemon.\n\n\n**Implementing Relational Persistence**\n\nI\'ve decided to implement a repository pattern. My aim is to make the application fully functional with CRUD, auth, and persistence, whether connected to MySQL in production or using a fallback relational store in development. I\'m exploring a setup where `mysql2/promise` handles MySQL 8 connections when credentials are provided, but seamlessly defaults to SQLite or an in-memory SQL store for the sandbox environment, ensuring seamless operation.\n\n\n"
