    end_line: 1245
    content: "Act as a senior full-stack architect, React developer, Node.js developer, UI/UX designer, database engineer, DevOps engineer, and n8n automation specialist.\r\n\r\nBuild a complete, production-ready social-media automation dashboard named:\r\n\r\nCI360 AUTOMATION HUB\r\n\r\nThe dashboard must connect securely to existing n8n workflows and allow users to create, approve, schedule, monitor, and report social-media posts from one interface.\r\n\r\nIMPORTANT RULES\r\n\r\n1. Do not recreate n8n\342\200\231s visual workflow editor.\r\n2. The dashboard must control n8n using:\r\n   - Production webhook URLs for business actions\r\n   - n8n REST API for workflows and executions\r\n3. Never expose the n8n API key, webhook secret, database credentials, or platform access tokens in React.\r\n4. All protected communication must pass through the Node.js backend.\r\n5. Do not hardcode mock data in production pages.\r\n6. Use a real MySQL database.\r\n7. Build responsive layouts for desktop, tablet, and mobile.\r\n8. Use only open-source packages unless clearly documented.\r\n9. Preserve clean separation between frontend, backend, database, and n8n integrations.\r\n10. Generate the complete project, not only a UI demonstration.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n1. TECHNOLOGY STACK\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nFrontend:\r\n- React 19\r\n- Vite\r\n- TypeScript\r\n- React Router\r\n- Tailwind CSS\r\n- shadcn/ui\r\n- TanStack Query\r\n- React Hook Form\r\n- Zod validation\r\n- Recharts\r\n- Lucide React icons\r\n- Socket.IO Client\r\n- date-fns\r\n- Axios or Fetch wrapper\r\n\r\nBackend:\r\n- Node.js\r\n- Express.js\r\n- TypeScript\r\n- MySQL 8\r\n- mysql2 connection pool\r\n- Socket.IO\r\n- JWT access and refresh tokens\r\n- HTTP-only secure cookies\r\n- Argon2id password hashing\r\n- Zod request validation\r\n- Helmet\r\n- CORS\r\n- Express Rate Limit\r\n- Pino structured logging\r\n- Multer for controlled uploads\r\n- Nodemailer for alerts\r\n- node-cron only for dashboard maintenance tasks, not social posting\r\n\r\nAutomation:\r\n- Existing self-hosted n8n instance\r\n- n8n production webhooks\r\n- n8n REST API\r\n- Google Sheets integration\r\n- Email approval integration\r\n- Social-platform nodes or API requests inside n8n\r\n\r\nHosting target:\r\n- React and Node.js Web App on Hostinger\r\n- Hostinger MySQL database\r\n- HTTPS domain\r\n- n8n may be hosted separately on a VPS or supported Node environment\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n2. PROJECT ARCHITECTURE\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate a monorepo:\r\n\r\nci360-automation-hub/\r\n  client/\r\n  server/\r\n  database/\r\n  docs/\r\n  .env.example\r\n  package.json\r\n  README.md\r\n\r\nFrontend structure:\r\n\r\nclient/src/\r\n  api/\r\n  assets/\r\n  components/\r\n  features/\r\n    auth/\r\n    dashboard/\r\n    posts/\r\n    approvals/\r\n    calendar/\r\n    brands/\r\n    accounts/\r\n    workflows/\r\n    executions/\r\n    reports/\r\n    notifications/\r\n    settings/\r\n  hooks/\r\n  layouts/\r\n  pages/\r\n  routes/\r\n  schemas/\r\n  stores/\r\n  styles/\r\n  types/\r\n  utils/\r\n\r\nBackend structure:\r\n\r\nserver/src/\r\n  config/\r\n  controllers/\r\n  middleware/\r\n  routes/\r\n  services/\r\n    auth/\r\n    n8n/\r\n    posts/\r\n    approvals/\r\n    reports/\r\n    notifications/\r\n  repositories/\r\n  sockets/\r\n  jobs/\r\n  validators/\r\n  utils/\r\n  types/\r\n  app.ts\r\n  server.ts\r\n\r\nUse feature-based modules and reusable components. Avoid oversized files and duplicate logic.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n3. USER ROLES AND PERMISSIONS\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate role-based access control.\r\n\r\nSuper Admin:\r\n- Full system access\r\n- Manage users, roles, brands, accounts, workflows and settings\r\n- View security and audit logs\r\n- Activate or deactivate integrations\r\n\r\nAdmin:\r\n- Manage brands and team members\r\n- Create and schedule posts\r\n- Approve or reject content\r\n- View all executions and reports\r\n- Retry failed jobs\r\n\r\nContent Manager:\r\n- Create and edit posts\r\n- Upload media\r\n- Generate or revise captions\r\n- Submit posts for approval\r\n- View assigned brands\r\n\r\nApprover:\r\n- View pending posts\r\n- Approve, reject or request revision\r\n- Add approval comments\r\n- View previous versions\r\n\r\nAnalyst:\r\n- Read-only access to analytics, reports and execution history\r\n\r\nClient:\r\n- View only assigned brands\r\n- Review and approve assigned content\r\n- Cannot view credentials, other brands or system settings\r\n\r\nEvery backend route must enforce authentication and permission checks.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n4. AUTHENTICATION\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate:\r\n\r\n- Login using email and password\r\n- Forgot-password flow\r\n- Secure password-reset token\r\n- Access token with a short expiration\r\n- Refresh token rotation\r\n- HTTP-only, Secure and SameSite cookies\r\n- Logout from current device\r\n- Logout from all devices\r\n- Account lockout after repeated failed attempts\r\n- Optional two-factor-authentication-ready architecture\r\n- Session list with device and last activity\r\n- Audit trail for login, logout and password changes\r\n\r\nNever store JWT tokens in localStorage.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n5. APPLICATION LAYOUT\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate a premium SaaS dashboard.\r\n\r\nVisual direction:\r\n- Professional digital-agency dashboard\r\n- Font: Poppins\r\n- Background: #F6F8FC\r\n- Main text: #101828\r\n- Muted text: #667085\r\n- Primary blue: #1336E8\r\n- Cyan accent: #08C5E1\r\n- Success: #12B76A\r\n- Warning: #F79009\r\n- Error: #F04438\r\n- White cards\r\n- Subtle borders and shadows\r\n- Rounded corners between 12px and 18px\r\n- Clear spacing and strong information hierarchy\r\n\r\nDesktop:\r\n- Collapsible left sidebar\r\n- Sticky top header\r\n- Main workspace\r\n- Optional right-side activity drawer\r\n\r\nMobile:\r\n- Compact top header\r\n- Drawer navigation\r\n- Bottom navigation for Dashboard, Calendar, Create, Approvals and More\r\n- Touch targets at least 44px\r\n- Tables change into readable cards\r\n\r\nSidebar navigation:\r\n- Overview\r\n- Content\r\n- Content Calendar\r\n- Create Post\r\n- Approval Queue\r\n- Published Posts\r\n- Brands\r\n- Social Accounts\r\n- Automations\r\n- Workflow Executions\r\n- Analytics\r\n- Reports\r\n- Notifications\r\n- Team\r\n- Audit Logs\r\n- Settings\r\n\r\nHeader:\r\n- Global search\r\n- Brand selector\r\n- Date-range selector\r\n- n8n connection indicator\r\n- Notification bell\r\n- User profile menu\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n6. OVERVIEW DASHBOARD\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nAdd KPI cards:\r\n\r\n- Posts scheduled\r\n- Posts published\r\n- Pending approvals\r\n- Rejected posts\r\n- Failed automations\r\n- Active workflows\r\n- Connected platforms\r\n- Total engagement\r\n\r\nAdd widgets:\r\n\r\n- Publishing performance chart\r\n- Posts by platform\r\n- Approval status breakdown\r\n- Upcoming scheduled posts\r\n- Recent automation executions\r\n- Failed executions requiring attention\r\n- Recent team activity\r\n- Platform connection health\r\n- Best-performing content\r\n- Brand performance selector\r\n\r\nFilters:\r\n- Brand\r\n- Platform\r\n- Country\r\n- Date range\r\n- Post status\r\n\r\nDo not use fake analytics in production. Show useful empty states until data is available.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n7. CONTENT MANAGEMENT\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate a central content table with:\r\n\r\n- Media thumbnail\r\n- Post title\r\n- Brand\r\n- Caption preview\r\n- Platform\r\n- Country/timezone\r\n- Scheduled date and time\r\n- Approval status\r\n- Publishing status\r\n- Assigned approver\r\n- Last updated\r\n- Actions menu\r\n\r\nContent statuses:\r\n\r\n- Draft\r\n- In Review\r\n- Revision Requested\r\n- Approved\r\n- Rejected\r\n- Scheduled\r\n- Processing\r\n- Published\r\n- Partially Published\r\n- Failed\r\n- Cancelled\r\n\r\nActions:\r\n- View\r\n- Edit\r\n- Duplicate\r\n- Submit for approval\r\n- Approve\r\n- Reject\r\n- Request revision\r\n- Schedule\r\n- Publish now\r\n- Cancel schedule\r\n- Retry\r\n- Archive\r\n\r\nInclude bulk actions with confirmation dialogs and authorization checks.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n8. CREATE POST SCREEN\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate a multi-step post composer.\r\n\r\nStep 1: Brand and campaign\r\n- Brand\r\n- Campaign\r\n- Post title\r\n- Internal tags\r\n- Country\r\n- Timezone\r\n\r\nStep 2: Platform selection\r\n- LinkedIn\r\n- Facebook\r\n- Instagram\r\n- X\r\n- Optional future YouTube support\r\n\r\nAllow selecting multiple platforms.\r\n\r\nStep 3: Media\r\n- Upload image or video\r\n- Import Google Drive public/share link\r\n- Media preview\r\n- File validation\r\n- Image aspect-ratio information\r\n- Video duration and size\r\n- Alt text\r\n- Remove or replace media\r\n\r\nStep 4: Caption\r\n- Master caption\r\n- Platform-specific caption overrides\r\n- Hashtags\r\n- Discovery keywords\r\n- Link\r\n- First comment\r\n- Character counters\r\n- Emoji support\r\n- Preview for each platform\r\n\r\nStep 5: Schedule\r\n- Publish now\r\n- Select date and time\r\n- Timezone\r\n- Repeat disabled by default\r\n- Prevent past dates\r\n- Warn about schedule conflicts\r\n\r\nStep 6: Approval\r\n- Assign approver\r\n- Add internal note\r\n- Submit for approval or save as draft\r\n\r\nUse autosave with visible \342\200\234Saved\342\200\235 status. Maintain version history for caption, media and schedule changes.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n9. WHATSAPP/INSTAGRAM-STYLE APPROVAL COMMENTS\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nInside each content item, create a chat-style discussion panel:\r\n\r\n- User avatars\r\n- Message bubbles\r\n- Timestamps\r\n- Read status\r\n- Typing indicator\r\n- Attachments\r\n- Mentions\r\n- Reply to message\r\n- Edit own recent comment\r\n- Delete according to permission\r\n- System messages for status changes\r\n- Real-time updates through Socket.IO\r\n\r\nThis is an internal approval conversation, not a public social-media chat.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n10. APPROVAL SYSTEM\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nApproval queue must include:\r\n\r\n- Pending review\r\n- Revision requested\r\n- Approved\r\n- Rejected\r\n- Overdue\r\n\r\nApproval detail page:\r\n- Full post preview\r\n- Master and platform-specific captions\r\n- Media preview\r\n- Schedule\r\n- Previous versions\r\n- Reviewer discussion\r\n- Approve button\r\n- Reject button requiring a reason\r\n- Request-revision button requiring comments\r\n- Reassign approver\r\n- Approval activity timeline\r\n\r\nRules:\r\n- Only authorized users can approve\r\n- Approved content becomes locked\r\n- Editing approved content returns it to review\r\n- Every change must be recorded\r\n- Publishing requires final approval unless a Super Admin overrides it\r\n- All overrides must be audited\r\n\r\nEmail approval links must use signed, expiring tokens. A user must authenticate before a final approval action.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n11. CONTENT CALENDAR\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate:\r\n- Month view\r\n- Week view\r\n- Day view\r\n- Agenda view\r\n\r\nCalendar features:\r\n- Platform icons\r\n- Brand colours\r\n- Status colours\r\n- Drag-and-drop rescheduling\r\n- Confirmation before changing approved content\r\n- Click to open details\r\n- Quick-create action\r\n- Filter by brand, platform, country and status\r\n- Detect schedule collisions\r\n- Display time in the selected timezone\r\n\r\nPersist schedule changes to MySQL and then call the appropriate n8n webhook.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n12. N8N INTEGRATION\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate a dedicated backend n8n service.\r\n\r\nEnvironment variables:\r\n\r\nN8N_BASE_URL=\r\nN8N_API_KEY=\r\nN8N_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL=\r\nN8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET=\r\nN8N_TIMEOUT_MS=15000\r\n\r\nBackend responsibilities:\r\n- Validate user permissions\r\n- Validate and sanitize webhook payloads\r\n- Attach webhook authentication\r\n- Set an idempotency key\r\n- Call n8n\r\n- Handle timeouts\r\n- Retry only safe operations\r\n- Store the external execution ID\r\n- Normalize n8n responses\r\n- Log success and failure safely\r\n- Never log secrets or tokens\r\n\r\nCreate webhook mappings:\r\n\r\nPOST /api/automations/create-post\r\n\342\206\222 /webhook/ci360/create-post\r\n\r\nPOST /api/automations/request-approval\r\n\342\206\222 /webhook/ci360/request-approval\r\n\r\nPOST /api/automations/revise-post\r\n\342\206\222 /webhook/ci360/revise-post\r\n\r\nPOST /api/automations/schedule-post\r\n\342\206\222 /webhook/ci360/schedule-post\r\n\r\nPOST /api/automations/publish-now\r\n\342\206\222 /webhook/ci360/publish-now\r\n\r\nPOST /api/automations/retry-publication\r\n\342\206\222 /webhook/ci360/retry-publication\r\n\r\nPOST /api/integrations/n8n/callback\r\n\342\206\222 Receive secured n8n execution updates\r\n\r\nEach outbound request must contain:\r\n\r\n{\r\n  \"requestId\": \"UUID\",\r\n  \"idempotencyKey\": \"UUID\",\r\n  \"postId\": 123,\r\n  \"brandId\": 10,\r\n  \"requestedBy\": 7,\r\n  \"timestamp\": \"ISO_DATE\",\r\n  \"data\": {}\r\n}\r\n\r\nSecure webhooks using an HMAC SHA-256 signature and timestamp. Reject callbacks with an invalid signature or stale timestamp.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n13. N8N WORKFLOW BEHAVIOUR\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nThe primary workflow should:\r\n\r\n1. Receive a webhook request.\r\n2. Verify the secret/signature.\r\n3. Validate required fields.\r\n4. Retrieve the approved post.\r\n5. Confirm the post is still approved.\r\n6. Retrieve media securely.\r\n7. Prepare platform-specific payloads.\r\n8. Publish to every selected platform.\r\n9. Capture the response for each platform.\r\n10. Update the dashboard through a callback webhook.\r\n11. Write reporting information to MySQL or Google Sheets.\r\n12. Send success/failure notifications.\r\n13. Return an execution ID immediately for long-running jobs.\r\n\r\nUse one parent orchestration workflow and separate sub-workflows for:\r\n- LinkedIn publishing\r\n- Facebook publishing\r\n- Instagram publishing\r\n- X publishing\r\n- Email approval\r\n- Google Sheets synchronization\r\n- Reporting\r\n- Failure notification\r\n\r\nA failure on one platform must not erase successful results from other platforms. Save per-platform results.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n14. GOOGLE SHEETS INTEGRATION\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nSupport importing and synchronizing a planning sheet with columns:\r\n\r\n- external_id\r\n- post_url\r\n- media_url\r\n- brand\r\n- campaign\r\n- platform\r\n- country\r\n- timezone\r\n- schedule_time\r\n- caption\r\n- hashtags\r\n- keywords\r\n- approval_status\r\n- rejection_reason\r\n- publishing_status\r\n- published_url\r\n- execution_id\r\n- error_message\r\n- updated_at\r\n\r\nRequirements:\r\n- Avoid duplicate imports using external_id\r\n- Validate dates and required fields\r\n- Mark invalid rows\r\n- Sync dashboard changes safely\r\n- Keep MySQL as the application source of truth\r\n- Use Google Sheets as an import/export and collaboration channel\r\n- Record last synchronization time\r\n- Show row-level sync errors\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n15. AUTOMATIONS PAGE\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nDisplay:\r\n- Workflow name\r\n- n8n workflow ID\r\n- Active/inactive status\r\n- Last execution\r\n- Last result\r\n- Success rate\r\n- Average duration\r\n- Failure count\r\n- Associated brands\r\n- Available action\r\n\r\nActions:\r\n- Execute supported workflow\r\n- View executions\r\n- Activate/deactivate if permitted\r\n- Open workflow in n8n\r\n- Test connection\r\n- Retry a failed execution\r\n\r\nDo not allow arbitrary workflow execution. Maintain an allowlist of dashboard-accessible workflow IDs.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n16. EXECUTION MONITORING\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nExecution list:\r\n- Execution ID\r\n- Workflow\r\n- Post\r\n- Brand\r\n- Trigger type\r\n- Started time\r\n- Finished time\r\n- Duration\r\n- Status\r\n- Initiated by\r\n\r\nStatuses:\r\n- Queued\r\n- Running\r\n- Success\r\n- Partial Success\r\n- Failed\r\n- Cancelled\r\n\r\nExecution detail:\r\n- Sanitized input\r\n- Workflow progress timeline\r\n- Per-platform results\r\n- Published links\r\n- Error summary\r\n- Retry action\r\n- Related post\r\n- Raw JSON for administrators only\r\n\r\nUse Socket.IO to update execution status without refreshing the page.\r\n\r\nDo not expose credentials, request authorization headers, access tokens or sensitive node data.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n17. SOCIAL ACCOUNT MANAGEMENT\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate a connection screen for:\r\n- LinkedIn\r\n- Facebook\r\n- Instagram\r\n- X\r\n\r\nDisplay:\r\n- Platform\r\n- Account/page name\r\n- Profile image\r\n- Connection status\r\n- Token expiry status\r\n- Last successful publication\r\n- Last error\r\n- Reconnect button\r\n- Disconnect button\r\n\r\nStore credentials encrypted at rest or keep them only inside n8n\342\200\231s credentials manager. Prefer n8n credential management. Never return tokens to the browser.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n18. BRANDS MANAGEMENT\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nBrand fields:\r\n- Name\r\n- Slug\r\n- Logo\r\n- Primary colour\r\n- Secondary colour\r\n- Timezone\r\n- Country\r\n- Default approver\r\n- Default hashtags\r\n- Default keywords\r\n- Connected social accounts\r\n- Active status\r\n\r\nUsers must only see brands assigned to them unless they have global permission.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n19. ANALYTICS AND REPORTS\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nAnalytics:\r\n- Total published posts\r\n- Reach\r\n- Impressions\r\n- Engagement\r\n- Engagement rate\r\n- Likes\r\n- Comments\r\n- Shares\r\n- Saves\r\n- Clicks\r\n- Video views\r\n- Follower growth\r\n- Success/failure rate by platform\r\n- Approval turnaround time\r\n\r\nFilters:\r\n- Date range\r\n- Brand\r\n- Platform\r\n- Campaign\r\n- Country\r\n\r\nReports:\r\n- Daily report\r\n- Weekly report\r\n- Monthly report\r\n- Brand report\r\n- Platform report\r\n- Automation-health report\r\n\r\nAllow exports:\r\n- CSV\r\n- XLSX\r\n- PDF\r\n\r\nClearly label missing or unavailable platform metrics. Never manufacture performance figures.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n20. NOTIFICATIONS\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate:\r\n- In-app notifications\r\n- Email notifications\r\n- Optional webhook notifications\r\n\r\nEvents:\r\n- Post submitted\r\n- Approval requested\r\n- Post approved\r\n- Post rejected\r\n- Revision requested\r\n- Post scheduled\r\n- Post published\r\n- Partial failure\r\n- Complete failure\r\n- Token expiry warning\r\n- Workflow disconnected\r\n\r\nSupport read/unread state and notification preferences.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n21. DATABASE SCHEMA\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate migrations and indexes for:\r\n\r\nusers\r\nroles\r\npermissions\r\nuser_roles\r\nrole_permissions\r\nrefresh_tokens\r\npassword_reset_tokens\r\nbrands\r\nbrand_users\r\nsocial_accounts\r\ncampaigns\r\nposts\r\npost_platforms\r\npost_media\r\npost_versions\r\npost_comments\r\npost_approvals\r\npost_schedules\r\nworkflow_mappings\r\nworkflow_executions\r\nplatform_publications\r\nanalytics_snapshots\r\nnotifications\r\nwebhook_events\r\nidempotency_keys\r\naudit_logs\r\napp_settings\r\n\r\nImportant relationships:\r\n- A post belongs to a brand.\r\n- A post can target multiple platforms.\r\n- A post can contain multiple media items.\r\n- Every edit creates a version.\r\n- Each platform publication has an independent result.\r\n- Every sensitive action creates an audit record.\r\n\r\nAdd indexes for:\r\n- Email\r\n- Brand ID\r\n- Status\r\n- Scheduled time\r\n- Platform\r\n- External execution ID\r\n- Created date\r\n- Idempotency key\r\n\r\nStore all database timestamps in UTC. Convert them for display using the selected timezone.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n22. API ROUTES\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate versioned routes under /api/v1.\r\n\r\nAuthentication:\r\nPOST /auth/login\r\nPOST /auth/refresh\r\nPOST /auth/logout\r\nPOST /auth/forgot-password\r\nPOST /auth/reset-password\r\nGET  /auth/me\r\n\r\nPosts:\r\nGET    /posts\r\nPOST   /posts\r\nGET    /posts/:id\r\nPATCH  /posts/:id\r\nDELETE /posts/:id\r\nPOST   /posts/:id/duplicate\r\nPOST   /posts/:id/submit\r\nPOST   /posts/:id/approve\r\nPOST   /posts/:id/reject\r\nPOST   /posts/:id/request-revision\r\nPOST   /posts/:id/schedule\r\nPOST   /posts/:id/publish\r\nPOST   /posts/:id/retry\r\nGET    /posts/:id/versions\r\nGET    /posts/:id/comments\r\nPOST   /posts/:id/comments\r\n\r\nBrands:\r\nGET    /brands\r\nPOST   /brands\r\nGET    /brands/:id\r\nPATCH  /brands/:id\r\nDELETE /brands/:id\r\n\r\nWorkflows:\r\nGET  /workflows\r\nGET  /workflows/:id\r\nPOST /workflows/:id/execute\r\nPOST /workflows/:id/activate\r\nPOST /workflows/:id/deactivate\r\nGET  /workflows/:id/executions\r\n\r\nExecutions:\r\nGET  /executions\r\nGET  /executions/:id\r\nPOST /executions/:id/retry\r\n\r\nReports:\r\nGET  /analytics/overview\r\nGET  /analytics/platforms\r\nGET  /analytics/content\r\nPOST /reports/generate\r\nGET  /reports/:id/download\r\n\r\nIntegrations:\r\nPOST /integrations/google-sheets/import\r\nPOST /integrations/google-sheets/sync\r\nPOST /integrations/n8n/test\r\nPOST /integrations/n8n/callback\r\n\r\nUse pagination, sorting, filtering and consistent response structures.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n23. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nImplement:\r\n- Argon2id password hashing\r\n- JWT rotation\r\n- HTTP-only cookies\r\n- CSRF protection where appropriate\r\n- Strict CORS allowlist\r\n- Helmet security headers\r\n- Rate limiting\r\n- Login-specific rate limiting\r\n- Request size limits\r\n- Zod validation\r\n- SQL parameterization\r\n- XSS-safe rendering\r\n- File MIME inspection\r\n- File size restrictions\r\n- Randomized upload names\r\n- Private upload directory\r\n- Signed media URLs\r\n- HMAC webhook verification\r\n- Replay-attack protection\r\n- Idempotency protection\r\n- Encrypted sensitive configuration\r\n- Audit logging\r\n- No secrets in frontend builds\r\n- No sensitive values in logs\r\n- Authorization on every resource\r\n- Brand-level tenant isolation\r\n\r\nProvide .env.example using placeholders only. Never commit actual secrets.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n24. RELIABILITY\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nImplement:\r\n- MySQL connection pooling\r\n- Transactions for approval and scheduling operations\r\n- Idempotent publishing\r\n- Structured error handling\r\n- Request IDs\r\n- Graceful server shutdown\r\n- Health checks\r\n- Readiness checks\r\n- Automatic safe retries with exponential backoff\r\n- Dead-letter/failure tracking\r\n- Duplicate-publishing prevention\r\n- Partial-success handling\r\n- Pagination for large datasets\r\n\r\nHealth endpoints:\r\nGET /health\r\nGET /ready\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n25. PERFORMANCE AND ACCESSIBILITY\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nPerformance:\r\n- Route-based code splitting\r\n- Lazy loading\r\n- Optimized images\r\n- WebP/AVIF previews\r\n- Paginated tables\r\n- Debounced search\r\n- Query caching\r\n- Avoid unnecessary React renders\r\n- Database query indexes\r\n- Skeleton loading states\r\n\r\nAccessibility:\r\n- WCAG 2.2 AA target\r\n- Keyboard navigation\r\n- Visible focus states\r\n- Semantic HTML\r\n- Form labels and descriptions\r\n- Accessible dialogs\r\n- Sufficient colour contrast\r\n- Screen-reader status messages\r\n- Reduced-motion support\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n26. TESTING\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nAdd:\r\n- Backend unit tests\r\n- API integration tests\r\n- Frontend component tests\r\n- Authentication tests\r\n- Permission tests\r\n- Approval-flow tests\r\n- Scheduling tests\r\n- Webhook-signature tests\r\n- Idempotency tests\r\n- n8n timeout/failure tests\r\n- End-to-end tests using Playwright\r\n\r\nCritical E2E flow:\r\n\r\nLogin\r\n\342\206\222 create post\r\n\342\206\222 upload media\r\n\342\206\222 select platforms\r\n\342\206\222 submit for approval\r\n\342\206\222 approve\r\n\342\206\222 schedule\r\n\342\206\222 trigger n8n\r\n\342\206\222 receive callback\r\n\342\206\222 show published/failed result\r\n\342\206\222 view report\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n27. ENVIRONMENT FILE\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nGenerate this .env.example:\r\n\r\nNODE_ENV=development\r\nPORT=3000\r\nCLIENT_URL=http://localhost:5173\r\nAPP_URL=http://localhost:3000\r\n\r\nDB_HOST=127.0.0.1\r\nDB_PORT=3306\r\nDB_NAME=ci360_automation\r\nDB_USER=\r\nDB_PASSWORD=\r\nDB_CONNECTION_LIMIT=5\r\n\r\nJWT_ACCESS_SECRET=\r\nJWT_REFRESH_SECRET=\r\nACCESS_TOKEN_TTL=15m\r\nREFRESH_TOKEN_TTL=30d\r\n\r\nCOOKIE_NAME=ci360_session\r\nCOOKIE_SECURE=false\r\nCOOKIE_SAME_SITE=lax\r\n\r\nN8N_BASE_URL=\r\nN8N_API_KEY=\r\nN8N_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL=\r\nN8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET=\r\nN8N_TIMEOUT_MS=15000\r\n\r\nUPLOAD_DIR=./data/private-uploads\r\nMAX_IMAGE_MB=8\r\nMAX_VIDEO_MB=50\r\nMAX_DOCUMENT_MB=15\r\n\r\nSMTP_HOST=\r\nSMTP_PORT=587\r\nSMTP_USER=\r\nSMTP_PASSWORD=\r\nSMTP_FROM=\r\n\r\nLOG_LEVEL=info\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n28. HOSTINGER DEPLOYMENT\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nPrepare deployment instructions for a Hostinger Node.js Web App:\r\n\r\n1. Build the React frontend.\r\n2. Serve client/dist from Express in production.\r\n3. Compile the server TypeScript into server/dist.\r\n4. Use the correct entry file:\r\n   server/dist/server.js\r\n5. Confirm server/tsconfig.json contains:\r\n\r\n{\r\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\r\n    \"rootDir\": \"./src\",\r\n    \"outDir\": \"./dist\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n6. Add scripts:\r\n\r\n\"build\": \"npm run build -w client && npm run build -w server\"\r\n\"start\": \"node server/dist/server.js\"\r\n\r\n7. Include:\r\n   - Environment import file\r\n   - MySQL import SQL\r\n   - Hostinger startup instructions\r\n   - Domain and HTTPS configuration\r\n   - SPA routing fallback\r\n   - Upload-directory permissions\r\n   - Production CORS configuration\r\n   - n8n callback URL configuration\r\n\r\nIf persistent Socket.IO connections are unsupported by the selected shared-hosting plan, use short polling for dashboard execution updates or recommend moving the Node/n8n services to a VPS. Do not silently assume WebSocket support.\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n29. REQUIRED DOCUMENTATION\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nCreate:\r\n\r\nREADME.md\r\ndocs/INSTALLATION.md\r\ndocs/HOSTINGER_DEPLOYMENT.md\r\ndocs/N8N_SETUP.md\r\ndocs/GOOGLE_SHEETS_SETUP.md\r\ndocs/SOCIAL_ACCOUNT_SETUP.md\r\ndocs/API.md\r\ndocs/SECURITY.md\r\ndocs/USER_GUIDE.md\r\ndocs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md\r\n\r\nExplain:\r\n- Installation\r\n- Database migration\r\n- Creating the first admin\r\n- Connecting n8n\r\n- Mapping allowed workflows\r\n- Creating webhook secrets\r\n- Google OAuth setup\r\n- Social account connections\r\n- Hostinger deployment\r\n- Backup and recovery\r\n- Token renewal\r\n- Common errors\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n30. DELIVERY REQUIREMENTS\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nDeliver:\r\n- Complete working source code\r\n- React dashboard\r\n- Node.js API\r\n- MySQL schema and migrations\r\n- n8n integration layer\r\n- Seed script with a development admin only\r\n- Responsive UI\r\n- Test suite\r\n- Deployment instructions\r\n- Environment example\r\n- API documentation\r\n- No TypeScript errors\r\n- No broken imports\r\n- No hardcoded secrets\r\n- No placeholder buttons\r\n- No fake successful operations\r\n- No unfinished TODO items in critical flows\r\n\r\nBefore declaring completion, run:\r\n\r\nnpm install\r\nnpm run lint\r\nnpm run typecheck\r\nnpm run test\r\nnpm run build\r\n\r\nVerify that:\r\n- client/dist exists\r\n- server/dist exists\r\n- server/dist/server.js exists\r\n- Production start command works\r\n- Login works\r\n- Permissions work\r\n- Post approval works\r\n- Schedule validation works\r\n- n8n test connection works\r\n- Webhook callback verification works\r\n- Execution statuses update correctly\r\n- No credentials appear in the browser bundle\r\n\r\n==================================================\r\n31. IMPLEMENTATION ORDER\r\n==================================================\r\n\r\nBuild the application in these phases:\r\n\r\nPhase 1:\r\n- Project setup\r\n- Database\r\n- Authentication\r\n- Roles and permissions\r\n- Base dashboard layout\r\n\r\nPhase 2:\r\n- Brands\r\n- Users\r\n- Content creation\r\n- Media handling\r\n- Content calendar\r\n\r\nPhase 3:\r\n- Approval workflow\r\n- Version history\r\n- Comments\r\n- Notifications\r\n\r\nPhase 4:\r\n- n8n webhooks\r\n- n8n API\r\n- Workflow execution monitoring\r\n- Secure callbacks\r\n\r\nPhase 5:\r\n- Google Sheets synchronization\r\n- Social account status\r\n- Analytics and reports\r\n\r\nPhase 6:\r\n- Testing\r\n- Security review\r\n- Performance optimization\r\n- Hostinger deployment documentation\r\n\r\nAt the end of every phase:\r\n1. Show created files.\r\n2. Explain database changes.\r\n3. List completed features.\r\n4. Run applicable tests.\r\n5. Fix all errors before continuing.\r\n6. Do not erase or overwrite completed working functionality.\r\n\r\nStart by inspecting the current repository. If it contains an existing project, document its structure and preserve any working configuration unless explicitly instructed to replace it. Then create a concise implementation plan and begin Phase 1."
