  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Automation Hub**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the scope for \"CI360 AUTOMATION HUB.\" This needs to be a production-ready dashboard. It should securely link to existing n8n workflows. The goal is to allow users to handle all aspects of social media from this single interface: create, approve, schedule, monitor, and report. This includes addressing the initial challenge of user instruction, and how to best deliver on it.\n\n\n**Refining Architecture Guidelines**\n\nI\'m now solidifying key architectural guardrails. My focus is avoiding recreating n8n\'s visual editor, instead leaning on its REST API and webhooks. I\'m prioritizing security by routing all protected communication through the backend, never hardcoding data, and ensuring a separation of concerns. Additionally, I need a responsive design and an implementation plan, starting with a repository inspection.\n\n\n**Examining Project Setup**\n\nI\'m now examining the workspace structure within AI Studio. I\'ve noted the development server at port 3000, and identified the primary tech stack: Vite, React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Express. I\'m structuring the codebase for the **CI360 AUTOMATION HUB** full-stack application. I\'ve defined Express routes for authentication, posts, brands, social accounts, workflows, executions, and analytics, ensuring a clean API design.\n\n\n**Analyzing API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now diving into the API endpoints. I\'ve mapped `/api/v1/analytics/*`, `/api/v1/reports/*`, and crucial integrations like Google Sheets and n8n webhooks with HMAC SHA-256 verification and encryption. The `/health` and `/ready` endpoints are also in focus. The database persistence layer, including `schema.sql` (MySQL 8 DDL with all 28 tables) and the `db.ts` file using `mysql2/promise` with auto-synchronization, is taking shape, and includes a seed admin user and sample data. I\'m noting the frontend\'s styling specification, which includes color definitions for visual consistency, as well.\n\n\n**Visualizing Frontend Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the user interface details. The error color will be #F04438, the font is Poppins, and I\'m using rounded corners from 12px to 18px. Cards will be white with subtle borders and shadows. I\'m also now visualizing a full navigation structure, with sections for dashboards, content management, a multi-step post composer, content calendar, and approval queue. There will also be areas for brand and social account management, automation workflows, executions, analytics, and team roles.\n\n\n**Defining Access & Files**\n\nI\'m now detailing user roles and their permissions, including an audit log for security. I\'m also creating the necessary monorepo files, database migrations, documentation, and Hostinger deployment scripts as requested, focusing on their specific contents. I\'m verifying the `metadata.json` and `index.html` files, ensuring the HTML title and meta descriptions are in sync with the metadata, and reflecting the required permissions and capabilities.\n\n\n"
