  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Backend Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the Express backend functions in a development environment that uses Vite. The AI Studio instructions are clear: a `server.ts` entry point is the way to go, running Express with `vite.middlewares` for development. It\'s crucial, according to the instructions, to avoid mounting Express within Vite itself.\n\n\n**Examining Build Configuration**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `server.ts` file, and noticed the conditional logic for production vs. development environments, and I see how Vite\'s middleware is used during development. The `package.json` file dictates the deployment steps, specifically with the `npm run build` command for deployment. I\'m focusing on ensuring these steps align with a full-stack deployment.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_588468"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import path from \'path\';\\nimport express from \'express\';\\nimport { createServer } from \'http\';\\nimport { app } from \'./server/src/app\';\\n\\nconst PORT = Number(process.env.PORT) || 3000;\\n\\nasync function startServer() {\\n  const isProd = process.env.NODE_ENV === \'production\';\\n\\n  if (!isProd) {\\n    // In dev, attach Vite middleware so frontend & backend run together on port 3000\\n    const { createServer: createViteServer } = await import(\'vite\');\\n    const vite = await createViteServer({\\n      server: { middlewareMode: true },\\n      appType: \'spa\',\\n    });\\n    app.use(vite.middlewares);\\n  } else {\\n    // In production, serve built SPA\\n    const distPath = path.resolve(process.cwd(), \'dist\');\\n    app.use(express.static(distPath));\\n    app.get(\'*\', (req, res) => {\\n      res.sendFile(path.join(distPath, \'index.html\'));\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  const server = createServer(app);\\n  server.listen(PORT, \'0.0.0.0\', () => {\\n    console.log(`CI360 Automation Hub running on http://0.0.0.0:${PORT}`);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nstartServer().catch(err => {\\n  console.error(\'Failed to start server:\', err);\\n  process.exit(1);\\n});\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create server.ts entry point mounting Express API routes and Vite dev middleware\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/server.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating server.ts entry point\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create server.ts\"}"
