  code_action {
    action_spec {
      create_file {
        instruction: "# CI360 Troubleshooting & Error Resolution\n\nGuide to diagnosing and resolving common operational issues.\n\n---\n\n## 1. n8n Webhook Timed Out (HTTP 504 / Connection Refused)\n\n- **Cause**: The self-hosted n8n instance is either stopped, blocked by firewall, or the `N8N_BASE_URL` is unreachable.\n- **Solution**:\n  1. Open the **Automations** tab in CI360.\n  2. Click **Test n8n Bridge** to verify network latency.\n  3. Confirm your n8n container is running (`docker ps`) and accessible over HTTPS.\n  4. Ensure `N8N_TIMEOUT_MS` in `.env` is set to at least 15000 (15s).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Webhook Callback Rejected (401 Unauthorized / Invalid Signature)\n\n- **Cause**: The HMAC SHA-256 signature generated by n8n does not match the server\'s `N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET` or the request timestamp is stale (>300 seconds).\n- **Solution**:\n  1. Verify the `N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET` matches across both `.env` and your n8n environment variables.\n  2. Check server time synchronization (NTP). Ensure system clocks are in sync.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hostinger Database Connection Limit Exceeded\n\n- **Cause**: Shared hosting plans limit concurrent MySQL connections per user.\n- **Solution**:\n  - In `server/src/config/db.ts`, ensure `connectionLimit` is set to `5` or lower.\n  - Check that all connections are properly released back to the pool after query execution.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Post Schedule Collisions\n\n- **Cause**: Multiple posts are queued to release at the exact same minute on the same brand channel.\n- **Solution**:\n  - Open the **Content Calendar** and look for amber collision badges.\n  - Stagger posts by at least 15 to 30 minutes to maximize audience engagement.\n"
        path {
          absolute_uri: "file:///docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md"
        }
        overwrite: true
      }
    }
    action_result {
      edit {
        diff {
          unified_diff {
