  planner_response {
    response: "# CI360 AUTOMATION HUB \342\200\224 Project Delivery Report\n\nA production-ready social media automation dashboard and orchestration bridge for self-hosted n8n workflows has been built and deployed. The platform enables marketing teams and agencies to create, approve, schedule, monitor, and report social posts from a unified interface with multi-tenant brand isolation.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project Architecture & Delivered Files\n\n```text\nci360-automation-hub/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 database/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 schema.sql              # Complete MySQL 8 schema (24 production tables & indexes)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 seeds.sql               # Default roles, Super Admin, brands, workflows, and sample posts\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 types/index.ts      # TypeScript definitions for entities, roles, and payloads\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 repositories/       # Relational repository with MySQL connection pooling\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 n8n/            # HMAC SHA-256 signing, idempotency, and REST API bridge\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.ts              # Express API v1 routes (/posts, /approvals, /workflows, etc.)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 api/client.ts           # Type-safe frontend API client\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/layout/      # Header with RBAC switcher & Collapsible Sidebar\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 features/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 dashboard/          # 8 KPI cards, platform health, and recent executions\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 posts/              # Content table & 6-step multi-channel post composer\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 approvals/          # Review queue with WhatsApp/Instagram-style chat\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 calendar/           # Month, Week, and Agenda views with collision detection\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 workflows/          # Allowed n8n workflows with test connection trigger\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 executions/         # Real-time execution logs, timeline, and retry actions\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 analytics/          # Cross-platform engagement charts & CSV reporting\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 sheets/             # 19-column Google Sheets bi-directional sync console\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 brands/             # Multi-tenant brand manager with custom color coding\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 accounts/           # LinkedIn, X, Facebook, and Instagram connection cards\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 audit/              # Immutable security & operational audit log\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 settings/           # Hostinger deployment guide & n8n secret manager\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 docs/                       # Complete production documentation suite (10 documents)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 .env.example                # Standard environment configuration template\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts                   # Production-ready entry point (Vite middleware in dev)\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 README.md                   # Project overview and quickstart guide\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Key Modules & Functional Implementation\n\n### A. Authentication & Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\n* **Predefined Roles**: Super Admin, Admin, Content Manager, Approver, Analyst, and Client.\n* **Tenant Isolation**: Users only view and manage brands assigned to them.\n* **Interactive RBAC Switcher**: The profile dropdown in the top header allows instant switching between roles to test permission boundaries in real time.\n* **Default Super Admin**:\n  * **Email**: `admin@ci360.internal`\n  * **Password**: `Admin@CI360#2026`\n\n### B. n8n Orchestration Bridge\n* **Protected Server-Side Communication**: No n8n API keys, database credentials, or platform access tokens are ever exposed to the React client.\n* **Signed Outbound Webhooks**: Every action dispatched to n8n is signed with an **HMAC SHA-256** signature over `${timestamp}.${rawBody}` using `N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET`.\n* **Idempotency & Tracing**: Includes `X-CI360-Request-Id` (UUIDv4) and `X-CI360-Idempotency-Key` to prevent double-publishing during network retries.\n* **Stale Callback Protection**: Inbound callbacks (`POST /api/v1/integrations/n8n/callback`) verify signature freshness within a 300-second window to prevent replay attacks.\n* **Allowed Workflow Mappings**:\n  1. `wf_ci360_multi_publisher` (`/webhook/ci360/publish-now`)\n  2. `wf_ci360_scheduler` (`/webhook/ci360/schedule-post`)\n  3. `wf_ci360_sheets_sync` (`/webhook/ci360/sync-sheets`)\n  4. `wf_ci360_approval_alert` (`/webhook/ci360/request-approval`)\n  5. `wf_ci360_revision` (`/webhook/ci360/revise-post`)\n\n### C. Multi-Step Post Composer (Create Post)\n* **Step 1 (Brand & Campaign)**: Brand selection, post title, campaign tag, country, and timezone.\n* **Step 2 (Platform Channels)**: Multi-selection across LinkedIn, X (Twitter), Facebook, and Instagram.\n* **Step 3 (Media Validation)**: File upload or Google Drive public link import, aspect ratio check (16:9 landscape verified), and accessibility alt text.\n* **Step 4 (Captions & Overrides)**: Master caption, platform-specific overrides (e.g. 280-character X summary), hashtags, target URL, and **live simulated card preview**.\n* **Step 5 (Schedule)**: Choose *Publish Immediately* or set future date/time with schedule collision warnings.\n* **Step 6 (Approval Routing)**: Assign reviewer (e.g. Marcus Sterling) with internal notes and submission status.\n\n### D. WhatsApp/Instagram-Style Review Discussion\n* **Real-time Discussion Stream**: Located directly inside the approval drawer with user avatars, message bubbles, timestamps, and double-check read indicators (`\342\234\223\342\234\223`).\n* **System Event Markers**: Automatically logs status transitions (e.g. `\342\232\231\357\270\217 Submitted post for final review`, `\342\232\231\357\270\217 Approved content for scheduling`).\n* **Formal Review Controls**:\n  * **Approve Content**: Locks the post from edits and queues it for automated publishing.\n  * **Request Revision**: Opens a comment dialog requiring specific modification notes.\n  * **Reject Post**: Enforces an explicit compliance or business reason recorded in the audit log.\n\n### E. Content Calendar\n* **Views**: Month, Week, and Agenda view modes.\n* **Collision Detection**: Flags schedule density collisions when multiple posts are queued within close proximity.\n* **Timezone Awareness**: Displays dates and release times aligned with brand timezones (`America/New_York`, `America/Los_Angeles`, `Europe/London`).\n\n### F. Hostinger Deployment & MySQL 8 Schema\n* **Complete DDL**: `database/schema.sql` creates all 24 production tables with `utf8mb4_unicode_ci` collation, foreign keys, and indexes.\n* **Hostinger Guide**: Detailed in `docs/HOSTINGER_DEPLOYMENT.md` for deploying to Hostinger Node.js Web Apps (configuring application root, `server/dist/server.js`, and environment variables).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Verification & Build Health\n\nThe application was validated using standard verification commands:\n\n```bash\nnpm run lint      # tsc --noEmit: Passed with 0 errors\nnpm run build     # Client SPA & Server compile: Succeeded\ncurl /health      # HTTP 200: {\"status\":\"healthy\",\"uptimeSeconds\":7}\n```\n\n*The CI360 Automation Hub is live on port 3000.*"
    thinking: "**Analyzing Current Status**\n\nI see the server is healthy, reporting an uptime of 7 seconds! Now, I\'m shifting focus to the project\'s requested structure. Specifically, I\'m working through the phases and deliverables, starting with the monorepo structure; the database schema is the first sub-item under consideration.\n\n\n**Defining Project Structure**\n\nI\'ve established the foundational components for the project\'s structure. I have a clear vision now of the database schema (`.sql` file including indexes, UTF8MB4, and constraints), the pre-seeded data, the Express API routes with authentication, the React dashboard with its specific styling, and comprehensive documentation covering installation, deployment, and usage, as well as included `.env.example` and `README.md` files. Moreover, the core features such as the overview dashboard, central content table, and multi-step post composer are fleshed out.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "# CI360 AUTOMATION HUB \342\200\224 Project Delivery Report\n\nA production-ready social media automation dashboard and orchestration bridge for self-hosted n8n workflows has been built and deployed. The platform enables marketing teams and agencies to create, approve, schedule, monitor, and report social posts from a unified interface with multi-tenant brand isolation.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project Architecture & Delivered Files\n\n```text\nci360-automation-hub/\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 database/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 schema.sql              # Complete MySQL 8 schema (24 production tables & indexes)\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 seeds.sql               # Default roles, Super Admin, brands, workflows, and sample posts\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 types/index.ts      # TypeScript definitions for entities, roles, and payloads\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 repositories/       # Relational repository with MySQL connection pooling\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 services/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 n8n/            # HMAC SHA-256 signing, idempotency, and REST API bridge\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 app.ts              # Express API v1 routes (/posts, /approvals, /workflows, etc.)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 src/\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 api/client.ts           # Type-safe frontend API client\n\342\224\202   \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 components/layout/      # Header with RBAC switcher & Collapsible Sidebar\n\342\224\202   \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 features/\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 dashboard/          # 8 KPI cards, platform health, and recent executions\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 posts/              # Content table & 6-step multi-channel post composer\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 approvals/          # Review queue with WhatsApp/Instagram-style chat\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 calendar/           # Month, Week, and Agenda views with collision detection\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 workflows/          # Allowed n8n workflows with test connection trigger\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 executions/         # Real-time execution logs, timeline, and retry actions\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 analytics/          # Cross-platform engagement charts & CSV reporting\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 sheets/             # 19-column Google Sheets bi-directional sync console\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 brands/             # Multi-tenant brand manager with custom color coding\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 accounts/           # LinkedIn, X, Facebook, and Instagram connection cards\n\342\224\202       \342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 audit/              # Immutable security & operational audit log\n\342\224\202       \342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 settings/           # Hostinger deployment guide & n8n secret manager\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 docs/                       # Complete production documentation suite (10 documents)\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 .env.example                # Standard environment configuration template\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200 server.ts                   # Production-ready entry point (Vite middleware in dev)\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200 README.md                   # Project overview and quickstart guide\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Key Modules & Functional Implementation\n\n### A. Authentication & Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)\n* **Predefined Roles**: Super Admin, Admin, Content Manager, Approver, Analyst, and Client.\n* **Tenant Isolation**: Users only view and manage brands assigned to them.\n* **Interactive RBAC Switcher**: The profile dropdown in the top header allows instant switching between roles to test permission boundaries in real time.\n* **Default Super Admin**:\n  * **Email**: `admin@ci360.internal`\n  * **Password**: `Admin@CI360#2026`\n\n### B. n8n Orchestration Bridge\n* **Protected Server-Side Communication**: No n8n API keys, database credentials, or platform access tokens are ever exposed to the React client.\n* **Signed Outbound Webhooks**: Every action dispatched to n8n is signed with an **HMAC SHA-256** signature over `${timestamp}.${rawBody}` using `N8N_WEBHOOK_SECRET`.\n* **Idempotency & Tracing**: Includes `X-CI360-Request-Id` (UUIDv4) and `X-CI360-Idempotency-Key` to prevent double-publishing during network retries.\n* **Stale Callback Protection**: Inbound callbacks (`POST /api/v1/integrations/n8n/callback`) verify signature freshness within a 300-second window to prevent replay attacks.\n* **Allowed Workflow Mappings**:\n  1. `wf_ci360_multi_publisher` (`/webhook/ci360/publish-now`)\n  2. `wf_ci360_scheduler` (`/webhook/ci360/schedule-post`)\n  3. `wf_ci360_sheets_sync` (`/webhook/ci360/sync-sheets`)\n  4. `wf_ci360_approval_alert` (`/webhook/ci360/request-approval`)\n  5. `wf_ci360_revision` (`/webhook/ci360/revise-post`)\n\n### C. Multi-Step Post Composer (Create Post)\n* **Step 1 (Brand & Campaign)**: Brand selection, post title, campaign tag, country, and timezone.\n* **Step 2 (Platform Channels)**: Multi-selection across LinkedIn, X (Twitter), Facebook, and Instagram.\n* **Step 3 (Media Validation)**: File upload or Google Drive public link import, aspect ratio check (16:9 landscape verified), and accessibility alt text.\n* **Step 4 (Captions & Overrides)**: Master caption, platform-specific overrides (e.g. 280-character X summary), hashtags, target URL, and **live simulated card preview**.\n* **Step 5 (Schedule)**: Choose *Publish Immediately* or set future date/time with schedule collision warnings.\n* **Step 6 (Approval Routing)**: Assign reviewer (e.g. Marcus Sterling) with internal notes and submission status.\n\n### D. WhatsApp/Instagram-Style Review Discussion\n* **Real-time Discussion Stream**: Located directly inside the approval drawer with user avatars, message bubbles, timestamps, and double-check read indicators (`\342\234\223\342\234\223`).\n* **System Event Markers**: Automatically logs status transitions (e.g. `\342\232\231\357\270\217 Submitted post for final review`, `\342\232\231\357\270\217 Approved content for scheduling`).\n* **Formal Review Controls**:\n  * **Approve Content**: Locks the post from edits and queues it for automated publishing.\n  * **Request Revision**: Opens a comment dialog requiring specific modification notes.\n  * **Reject Post**: Enforces an explicit compliance or business reason recorded in the audit log.\n\n### E. Content Calendar\n* **Views**: Month, Week, and Agenda view modes.\n* **Collision Detection**: Flags schedule density collisions when multiple posts are queued within close proximity.\n* **Timezone Awareness**: Displays dates and release times aligned with brand timezones (`America/New_York`, `America/Los_Angeles`, `Europe/London`).\n\n### F. Hostinger Deployment & MySQL 8 Schema\n* **Complete DDL**: `database/schema.sql` creates all 24 production tables with `utf8mb4_unicode_ci` collation, foreign keys, and indexes.\n* **Hostinger Guide**: Detailed in `docs/HOSTINGER_DEPLOYMENT.md` for deploying to Hostinger Node.js Web Apps (configuring application root, `server/dist/server.js`, and environment variables).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Verification & Build Health\n\nThe application was validated using standard verification commands:\n\n```bash\nnpm run lint      # tsc --noEmit: Passed with 0 errors\nnpm run build     # Client SPA & Server compile: Succeeded\ncurl /health      # HTTP 200: {\"status\":\"healthy\",\"uptimeSeconds\":7}\n```\n\n*The CI360 Automation Hub is live on port 3000.*"
