  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n1. Task Overview\n- **User Request**: The user provided a screenshot of the \"Team & Role-Based Access Control\" screen in **CI360 AUTOMATION HUB** and requested:\n  1. Add full **Edit**, **Delete**, and **Add/Invite** team member capabilities (with roles: Super Admin, Admin, Content Manager, Approver, Analyst, Client; and tenant scope assignments).\n  2. Make the entire layout **mobile responsive** (hamburger/drawer navigation, mobile bottom action bar for navigation tabs, responsive tables converting to cards on small screens).\n  3. Ensure that **clicking anywhere outside hides the notification dropdown and user profile dropdown** (click-outside / backdrop dismiss handler).\n- **Core App**: Full-stack CI360 Automation Hub running on port 3000 (Express backend with `/api/v1/*` routes mounted via Vite middleware in `server.ts`).\n\n2. Progress\n- **Completed in Previous Turns**:\n  - Full backend Express API (`server/src/app.ts`), relational repository (`server/src/repositories/database.ts`), and types (`server/src/types/index.ts`).\n  - Core views: Overview Dashboard, Content Table, 6-step Create Post Composer, Approval Queue with WhatsApp-style chat, Content Calendar, Automations & n8n bridge, Executions log, Analytics, Sheets sync, Brands, Social Accounts, Audit Logs, Settings.\n  - Complete MySQL 8 schema (`database/schema.sql`) and seeds (`database/seeds.sql`).\n  - Full documentation (`docs/`).\n  - Verified with `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` (both passed with 0 errors).\n- **In Progress / Current Turn**:\n  - Enhancing `Team & RBAC` feature: currently in `src/App.tsx` (lines 350-388) it is a static table without Add, Edit, or Delete modals and actions. Needs its own modular feature component `src/features/team/TeamPage.tsx` with full CRUD (Add Member, Edit Member, Delete Member, Role change, Tenant scope assignment).\n  - Updating `src/components/layout/Header.tsx` to handle **click-outside dismissal** using `useEffect` with `document.addEventListener(\'mousedown\', ...)` on ref containers for both the Notification bell dropdown and the User profile/role dropdown.\n  - Updating mobile responsiveness: adding hamburger drawer for mobile view in `Header.tsx` / `Sidebar.tsx` and mobile bottom navigation bar in `src/components/layout/MobileNav.tsx`.\n\n3. Key Findings\n- In `src/components/layout/Header.tsx`, `isNotifOpen` and `isProfileOpen` currently toggle with simple `onClick` without outside click listeners. Adding `useRef` for each dropdown container + a global `mousedown` listener cleanly dismisses them when clicking anywhere outside.\n- The user screenshot explicitly highlights the **Team & Role-Based Access Control** page. The user wants actions (\"add edit delete etc\") for team members in that table.\n- `DatabaseRepository` in `server/src/repositories/database.ts` already has `getUsers()`, `getUserById()`, and user seeds. We should add `createUser()`, `updateUser()`, and `deleteUser()` methods to `DatabaseRepository`, expose them in `server/src/app.ts` (`POST /api/v1/users`, `PATCH /api/v1/users/:id`, `DELETE /api/v1/users/:id`), and wire them up in `src/api/client.ts`.\n- In mobile screens (`< md`), the sidebar is hidden or collapses; we must ensure a smooth mobile drawer toggle button in `Header` and a floating bottom navigation strip.\n\n4. Active Context\n- Server runs `tsx server.ts` on port 3000.\n- `package.json` dependencies: `lucide-react`, `motion`, `date-fns`, `express`, `react`, `react-dom`.\n- Dev server is responsive and healthy (`/health` returns status `healthy`).\n\n5. Next Steps\n1. **Database & API for Team Members**:\n   - Update `server/src/repositories/database.ts` to add `createUser`, `updateUser`, `deleteUser`.\n   - Update `server/src/app.ts` with:\n     - `GET /api/v1/users`\n     - `POST /api/v1/users`\n     - `PATCH /api/v1/users/:id`\n     - `DELETE /api/v1/users/:id`\n   - Update `src/api/client.ts` to export `getUsers`, `createUser`, `updateUser`, `deleteUser`.\n2. **Build `src/features/team/TeamPage.tsx`**:\n   - Dynamic table with Add Team Member button.\n   - Per-row actions: **Edit Member** (modal to update Name, Email, Role, Tenant Scope, Active status) and **Delete Member** (with confirmation dialog).\n   - Add Member modal with input validation.\n   - Responsive card layout on mobile view (`hidden sm:table`, cards on mobile).\n3. **Fix Header Click-Outside Dropdown Behavior**:\n   - In `src/components/layout/Header.tsx`, add `useRef` and `useEffect` listener to auto-close `isNotifOpen` and `isProfileOpen` whenever clicking outside either dropdown.\n   - Add mobile hamburger button to trigger mobile sidebar/drawer.\n4. **Mobile Responsiveness**:\n   - Create `src/components/layout/MobileNav.tsx` or update `Sidebar.tsx` to support a mobile overlay drawer with backdrop.\n   - Update `src/App.tsx` to mount `TeamPage` and render the mobile navigation bar.\n5. **Verify**:\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` to confirm 0 compilation/type errors.\n\n6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Do not introduce mock/broken stubs; wire real state through `api.client` and backend routes.\n- Adhere to the established color scheme (Background `#F6F8FC`, text `#101828`, primary `#1336E8`, cyan `#08C5E1`, success `#12B76A`, danger `#F04438`, font Poppins).\n- Zero-pill metadata discipline, WCAG compliance, and 44px+ touch targets on mobile.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 208
    user_requests: "Here is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(<App />);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"dist\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\342\200\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    user_requests: "install n8n"
    user_requests: "List the top 5 most useful n8n integrations for a developer. For each integration, briefly explain how it can be leveraged and provide a basic example workflow.\n\nSet up n8n on my system. Provide instructions for initial configuration and suggest a simple workflow to start with, such as syncing new contacts from a form to a CRM."
