  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Display**\n\nI\'ve been examining the user\'s screenshot and have identified a significant issue on the left side: a large, empty white space. I\'m focusing on the `div` element with specific classes: \"flex h-screen w-screen overflow-hidden bg\". I\'m trying to figure out what is generating this area. I also want to determine the cause of the rendering issue.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Cause**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `<aside>` element within the `Sidebar.tsx` component. It\'s the culprit, specifically when `isMobileOpen` is false. The crucial point is the missing `hidden` or `fixed` classes! Despite the `-translate-x-full` transform, the flex layout means this sidebar still occupies space, pushing the entire layout to the right and creating that blank area.\n\n\n**Addressing the Layout Issues**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the header and the \"Approval Queue\" card. I\'ve noted that the search bar is clipped and various elements are overlapping in the header. On smaller screens, something needs to hide or condense. Turning to the \"Approval Queue\" card, I see wrapping and overlapping text, along with squished buttons at the bottom. The core problem is still related to document flow.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of UI elements and their responsiveness. I\'m focusing on the tab filter buttons; they need a horizontal scroll on smaller screens or a responsive flex-wrap. I\'m also addressing the entire application, making sure that every view, from the sidebar to the mobile bottom nav, is optimized for different screen sizes. My goal is to streamline the mobile experience.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_308698"
