  planner_response {
    response: "### Responsive Layout Fixes Completed\n\n1. **Eliminated Left White Void (Sidebar Layout Fix)**:\n   - Fixed an issue where the collapsed sidebar on screens below `1024px` still occupied `256px` in document flow (via `-translate-x-full`), causing the entire layout to be pushed right with a giant empty white space on the left.\n   - Updated `Sidebar.tsx` to use `hidden lg:flex` when closed, freeing up 100% of the viewport width for mobile and tablet screens. When opened via the top-left hamburger button, it transitions smoothly as an overlay drawer (`fixed inset-y-0 left-0 z-50 w-72`) with a backdrop.\n\n2. **Cleaned Up Approval Queue & Review Card**:\n   - Resolved the awkward multi-line text wrapping on the brand label and author line (`NEXUS ENTERPRISE CLOUD` and `Created by Elena Rostova`).\n   - Restructured the post card header with `flex-col xl:flex-row` and `whitespace-nowrap` pills.\n   - Action buttons (`Request Revision`, `Reject`, `Approve Content`) now wrap responsively with full touch-friendly targets (38px+).\n   - Added a smooth horizontal scrolling strip for the queue tabs (`Pending Review`, `Revision Requested`, `Approved`, `Rejected`).\n\n3. **Header Responsive Spacing**:\n   - Streamlined the search bar to show on larger viewports (`hidden xl:block`), eliminating horizontal crowding on tablets (768px\342\200\2231024px) where the search bar was getting crushed to `\"Q Sec\"`.\n   - Compact brand selector and user profile avatar on smaller screens prevent horizontal overflow.\n\n4. **Multi-Screen Responsive Card Feeds**:\n   - Added mobile card feeds to **Content Management** (`ContentTable.tsx`), switching from the 9-column data table to touch cards on screens under 768px.\n   - Added horizontal scroll handling for the month view in **Content Calendar** to prevent day columns from collapsing on small screens."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Server Status**\n\nI see the server is healthy! I\'ve confirmed an issue in `Sidebar.tsx`. The `<aside>` element had an incorrect translation, causing a white margin. Fixing it required adjusting the conditional classes to ensure the sidebar displays correctly across all screen sizes.\n\n\n**Refining Layout Adaptations**\n\nI\'ve tackled that layout issue where the 256px column was pushing everything. Now, the `Sidebar.tsx` utilizes `hidden lg:flex` when closed, freeing up screen space. Opening it triggers a fixed overlay. I also fixed a squished header in the Approval Queue, re-architecting it with flexbox for better flow and responsiveness, including responsive action button wrapping and smooth scroll for tab filters. And, I\'ve hidden the search bar on smaller screens.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Responsive Layout Fixes Completed\n\n1. **Eliminated Left White Void (Sidebar Layout Fix)**:\n   - Fixed an issue where the collapsed sidebar on screens below `1024px` still occupied `256px` in document flow (via `-translate-x-full`), causing the entire layout to be pushed right with a giant empty white space on the left.\n   - Updated `Sidebar.tsx` to use `hidden lg:flex` when closed, freeing up 100% of the viewport width for mobile and tablet screens. When opened via the top-left hamburger button, it transitions smoothly as an overlay drawer (`fixed inset-y-0 left-0 z-50 w-72`) with a backdrop.\n\n2. **Cleaned Up Approval Queue & Review Card**:\n   - Resolved the awkward multi-line text wrapping on the brand label and author line (`NEXUS ENTERPRISE CLOUD` and `Created by Elena Rostova`).\n   - Restructured the post card header with `flex-col xl:flex-row` and `whitespace-nowrap` pills.\n   - Action buttons (`Request Revision`, `Reject`, `Approve Content`) now wrap responsively with full touch-friendly targets (38px+).\n   - Added a smooth horizontal scrolling strip for the queue tabs (`Pending Review`, `Revision Requested`, `Approved`, `Rejected`).\n\n3. **Header Responsive Spacing**:\n   - Streamlined the search bar to show on larger viewports (`hidden xl:block`), eliminating horizontal crowding on tablets (768px\342\200\2231024px) where the search bar was getting crushed to `\"Q Sec\"`.\n   - Compact brand selector and user profile avatar on smaller screens prevent horizontal overflow.\n\n4. **Multi-Screen Responsive Card Feeds**:\n   - Added mobile card feeds to **Content Management** (`ContentTable.tsx`), switching from the 9-column data table to touch cards on screens under 768px.\n   - Added horizontal scroll handling for the month view in **Content Calendar** to prevent day columns from collapsing on small screens."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 100939174
