    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Request:** \"add user image editable\" with an attached screenshot (`/public/assets/aistudio/image_b5ae0cc5.png`) showing the Team & RBAC table containing user avatars for David Vance, Elena Rostova, Marcus Sterling, and Sophia Al-Mansoor.\n- **Goal:** Enable user profile images / avatars to be editable:\n  1. In the **Edit Member Modal** and **Add Member Modal** (`src/features/team/TeamPage.tsx`), add an avatar editing feature (image URL input + file upload preview + preset avatar picker + click avatar to change image).\n  2. In the user list table / mobile cards, allow clicking directly on the avatar or an edit icon overlay on the avatar to change/upload the user\'s photo.\n  3. Update the backend API (`server/src/routes/api.ts`) and client (`src/api/client.ts` and `src/App.tsx`) to support updating `avatarUrl` in `POST /api/v1/users` and `PATCH /api/v1/users/:id`.\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed in Prior Turns:**\n  - Full responsive layout audit across all viewports (fixed Sidebar `-translate-x-full` leaving empty space by applying `hidden lg:flex` when closed; fixed Header element widths; added responsive cards for Content Table; resolved Approval Queue multi-line text wrapping).\n  - Implemented team CRUD backend endpoints (`GET`, `POST`, `PATCH`, `DELETE` on `/api/v1/users` in `server/src/routes/api.ts`).\n  - Added initial `TeamPage.tsx` with Add Member, Edit Member, and Delete Member modals.\n- **In Progress (To Be Done for This Turn):**\n  - Making the user avatar image editable in both the Add Member modal and Edit Member modal, as well as providing an inline avatar change trigger in the Team list.\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Architecture\n- **Data Model:**\n  - User model in `server/src/types.ts`:\n    ```ts\n    export interface User {\n      id: number;\n      email: string;\n      fullName: string;\n      avatarUrl?: string;\n      role: RoleName;\n      tenantScope: string;\n      isActive: boolean;\n      twoFactorEnabled?: boolean;\n      createdAt: string;\n    }\n    ```\n  - `server/src/routes/api.ts`:\n    - `POST /api/v1/users` takes `{ fullName, email, role, tenantScope, isActive, avatarUrl }`. Need to ensure `avatarUrl` is accepted and persisted.\n    - `PATCH /api/v1/users/:id` updates `user` properties. Verify `avatarUrl` is allowed in the update payload.\n  - `src/features/team/TeamPage.tsx`:\n    - State currently tracks `fullName`, `email`, `role`, `tenantScope`, `isActive`.\n    - Needs `avatarUrl` state in both `AddMemberModal` and `EditMemberModal`.\n    - Should include file upload (using `FileReader` / `readAsDataURL` for base64 or instant client preview) and image URL input, plus quick preset selection avatars.\n    - Hovering or tapping the avatar in the row should show a camera/pencil icon affordance with a direct file picker or trigger the Edit modal with focus on the avatar.\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- Frontend compiles cleanly (`npm run build` / `tsc --noEmit` pass with 0 errors).\n- Dev server running on `http://localhost:3000` with Express proxy backend (`server.ts`).\n- Active files to modify:\n  - `server/src/routes/api.ts` (ensure `avatarUrl` is saved and updated)\n  - `src/features/team/TeamPage.tsx` (add avatar uploader/editor to modals and table rows)\n  - `src/App.tsx` (ensure `handleAddUser` and `handleUpdateUser` pass `avatarUrl`)\n\n### 5. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Update `server/src/routes/api.ts`:**\n   - In `POST /api/v1/users`, accept `avatarUrl` from `req.body` (defaulting to a fallback avatar if omitted).\n   - In `PATCH /api/v1/users/:id`, accept `avatarUrl` in updates.\n2. **Update `src/App.tsx`:**\n   - In `handleAddUser`: include `avatarUrl?: string` in the param type and pass it to `api.createUser`.\n   - In `handleUpdateUser`: ensure `updates: Partial<User>` passes `avatarUrl`.\n3. **Update `src/features/team/TeamPage.tsx`:**\n   - In `AddMemberModal`: add avatar preview with an upload button (`<input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/*\">`) and an avatar URL text input, plus a few default preset avatar chips.\n   - In `EditMemberModal`: add the same avatar preview, file uploader, URL input, and clear/reset button.\n   - In the Table and Mobile Cards: add a camera/edit icon badge overlay on the avatar so clicking the avatar opens the image picker/editor directly.\n4. **Verification:**\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` to ensure zero compilation or type errors.\n   - Restart dev server via `restart_dev_server` if backend routes are modified.\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Must maintain clean anti-slop design and WCAG accessibility standards.\n- Avatar edit must support both file upload (reading image as data URL) and direct image URL input.\n- Do not break existing team role badges, tenant scopes, or active toggle functionality.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 208
    included_step_index_end: 334
    user_requests: "\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/Paste_October_23__2026_-_12_43PM_cdad85ed (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/Paste_October_23__2026_-_12_43PM_cdad85ed). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/Paste_October_23__2026_-_12_43PM_cdad85ed. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "add edit delete etc make mobile responsive and and if click any where notification dropdown hide and use dropdown hide\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/image_8da69e80.png (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/image_8da69e80.png). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/image_8da69e80.png. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    user_requests: "all screen  responsive\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/image_c98cab20.png (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/image_c98cab20.png). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/image_c98cab20.png. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
