  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Checking User States**\n\nI\'ve been examining how user information is handled within `Header.tsx`, specifically focusing on avatar updates. Passing `currentUser?: User` or `currentUserAvatar?: string` seems to provide immediate visual feedback upon profile image changes. This approach is much quicker!\n\n\n**Designing Image Editing**\n\nI\'m now detailing the user image editing flow. My focus is on making it quick and intuitive. The plan involves a direct click or hover action on avatars within both the desktop table and mobile cards, triggering an \"Edit User Photo\" modal. This `avatarModalUser` will offer immediate options: uploading a file (with format and size checks), entering an image URL with a preview, and selecting from a grid of preset avatars.\n\n\n**Refining Modal Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating avatar controls into multiple modal flows. I\'m focusing on consistency: the \"Edit Member Modal\" now features seamless avatar controls at the top. The \"Add Member Modal\" also includes a selector with instant preview. A new feature I\'ve added is that it will allow 1-click selection of preset URLs with face crops. Backend updates are also underway, specifically destructuring and passing `avatarUrl` from `req.body` to `db.createUser`.\n\n\n**Preparing Avatar Resources**\n\nI\'m now getting the avatar URL parameters correct and ensuring the necessary types include `avatarUrl?: string`. I am also adding new preset avatar options; I\'ve found eight clean, professional photos from Unsplash. I\'ve begun to source preset avatar URLs. I\'m focusing on ensuring these URL sources are solid and ready.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_435575"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"Description\":\"Pass avatarUrl when creating a new user in server/src/app.ts\", \"EndLine\":88, \"Instruction\":\"Extract avatarUrl from req.body and pass it into db.createUser\", \"ReplacementContent\":\"app.post(\'/api/v1/users\', (req: Request, res: Response) => {\\n  const { email, fullName, role, tenantScope, isActive, avatarUrl } = req.body;\\n  if (!email || !fullName) {\\n    return res.status(400).json({ error: \'Email and full name are required\' });\\n  }\\n\\n  const existing = db.getUserByEmail(email);\\n  if (existing) {\\n    return res.status(409).json({ error: \'A team member with this email already exists\' });\\n  }\\n\\n  const user = db.createUser({\\n    email,\\n    fullName,\\n    role: role || \'Content Manager\',\\n    tenantScope: tenantScope || \'Global (All Brands)\',\\n    isActive: isActive !== undefined ? isActive : true,\\n    avatarUrl,\\n  });\", \"StartLine\":68, \"TargetContent\":\"app.post(\'/api/v1/users\', (req: Request, res: Response) => {\\n  const { email, fullName, role, tenantScope, isActive } = req.body;\\n  if (!email || !fullName) {\\n    return res.status(400).json({ error: \'Email and full name are required\' });\\n  }\\n\\n  const existing = db.getUserByEmail(email);\\n  if (existing) {\\n    return res.status(409).json({ error: \'A team member with this email already exists\' });\\n  }\\n\\n  const user = db.createUser({\\n    email,\\n    fullName,\\n    role: role || \'Content Manager\',\\n    tenantScope: tenantScope || \'Global (All Brands)\',\\n    isActive: isActive !== undefined ? isActive : true,\\n  });\", \"TargetFile\":\"/server/src/app.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Updating server user creation endpoint\", \"toolSummary\":\"Update server user endpoint for avatarUrl\"}"
