  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Component Logic**\n\nI\'m currently updating `handleAddUser` in `App.tsx` to accept an optional `avatarUrl` string. I\'m also considering how to pass the current user\'s data. I\'m leaning toward using either the full `currentUser` object (found from `users` array) or, alternatively, just the `currentUserAvatar` derived from the `users` array, to a child component.\n\n\n**Implementing User Avatar**\n\nI\'ve just added `currentUser?: User;` to `HeaderProps` in `src/components/layout/Header.tsx`. I\'ve updated `Header.tsx` to conditionally render the avatar using `currentUser?.avatarUrl` or, if absent, initials.  This successfully links the user\'s state to the header. I\'m now reviewing `TeamPage.tsx` and its `onAddUser` method.\n\n\n**Adding Preset Avatars**\n\nI\'ve just defined `PRESET_AVATARS` with several image URLs, which I\'m now integrating. The avatars include `id`, `label`, and `url` properties for each. I\'m considering how to best provide these options during user creation. I will ensure the preset avatars are displayed in the form, in addition to the upload option.\n\n\n**Designing Avatar Modal**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a Quick Avatar Editor modal within `TeamPage.tsx`. The design includes a large circular preview and an \"Upload New Photo\" button with a custom file input. This is important for a more streamlined avatar update process. The upload will use `FileReader.readAsDataURL` to instantly update the preview. I\'m aiming for a quick, user-friendly experience.\n\n\n**Refining Modal UI**\n\nI\'m now implementing the new avatar modal UI. I\'ve added a preset grid with hover effects, an image URL input with live preview, and a \"Remove Photo\" button. The \"Save Avatar\" button will trigger `onUpdateUser` and close the modal. Both the \"Edit Member\" and \"Add Member\" modals will feature the new avatar controls. I\'m also adding hover effects to table rows, with a badge icon for avatar changes. I\'ve confirmed `lucide-react` has all required icons.\n\n\n"
