  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Login Options**\n\nI\'m currently exploring the existence of a \"direct n8n login page.\" My focus is on understanding if there\'s a dedicated page for direct user login, or a method to connect to n8n directly with credentials or API keys. I\'m investigating how users might bypass potential redirects, and connect directly to the service. I\'m also examining the available authentication mechanisms to see how to enable this connection.\n\n\n**Defining Login Method**\n\nI\'m now thinking about providing a dedicated \"Direct n8n Login\" page within the application itself. I envision this page mimicking an authentic n8n login, complete with branded aesthetics. Users would input the instance URL, credentials (email/password or API key), and have options like \"Remember this instance\" and a \"Test Connection & Authenticate\" button. I\'m also considering quick login profiles and a launch button for one-click access. Additional features include a session status inspector and webhook endpoint tester.\n\n\n"
