  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing n8n Login**\n\nI\'m making headway on the n8n login integration. I\'ve pinpointed the `onClick` event in `Header.tsx` that will trigger the modal\'s opening using the function `onOpenN8nStatus`. This function will be defined in `src/App.tsx` and sets the active tab. Finally, the \"Direct n8n Login\" navigation tab (with the n8n icon) will be added to the `Sidebar.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing the Login Interface**\n\nI\'m now diving into the \"Direct n8n Login Page\" design. I\'m focusing on incorporating the official n8n aesthetic, including their distinctive colors and logo.  I\'m also considering dual-mode support, presets for Instance URLs, and auto-fill credential options. Thinking of default usernames and how to validate custom inputs for URLs and email addresses.\n\n\n**Defining Login Behavior**\n\nI\'m now detailing the post-login states and actions. I envision a green \"Active n8n Session Connected\" banner with user details (email, role, instance version, latency, engine). I\'m thinking of direct action buttons to open the n8n web editor, launch an embedded canvas, inspect active workflows, and view live webhook endpoints. I\'m also planning the \"Remember Session\" checkbox, and a \"Sign in to n8n\" button with realistic loading.\n\n\n**Establishing Backend Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now implementing the backend proxy and authentication endpoints in `server/src/app.ts`. I\'m focusing on `/api/v1/n8n/login`, which will handle credential validation, token generation, and instance verification. The `/api/v1/n8n/session` endpoint will provide the current session state, and the `/api/v1/n8n/logout` to clear the session. I\'m also planning the design of the direct navigation access by adding a tab for \"Direct n8n Login\" with the n8n icon to `Sidebar.tsx`, and making the \"n8n Connected\" pill navigate to the login page.\n\n\n"
