  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Exceptional Login**\n\nI\'m focusing on crafting an exceptional direct n8n login page. The core features I\'m prioritizing are direct n8n authentication and establishing a robust gateway. I\'m exploring the specific elements that will make this page a top-tier user experience, ensuring it fully meets user needs.\n\n\n**Designing Login Details**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the design details of the authentication portal. I\'m focusing on incorporating the official n8n branding, including the coral gradient. I\'m thinking of headlines like \"Sign in to n8n Workflow Automation\" and a subtitle that covers different instance types. I\'m also planning an instance switcher with quick selector tabs and a visual connectivity indicator. The user will be able to easily log in using email and password, plus a \"stay signed in\" feature.\n\n\n**Expanding Login Options**\n\nI\'m now adding API key/secret token login with a \"Fill Demo Key\" or \"Generate Test Token\" option. I\'m also including a 1-click SSO option to open the authenticated app in a new tab, and an embed preview toggle. Finally, I\'m conceptualizing a post-authentication status panel.\n\n\n**Implementing Login Support**\n\nI\'m now focused on implementing robust backend and client API support. I\'m building out `/api/v1/n8n/auth`, `/api/v1/n8n/session`, and `/api/v1/n8n/logout` endpoints, along with corresponding client functions in `src/api/client.ts`. I\'m also planning to incorporate a navigation item for the login feature in `Sidebar.tsx`, complete with a badge. I\'m designing 1-click credential cards with example admin/cloud credentials and related copyable CLI commands for n8n.\n\n\n"
