  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Request**: `\"n8n with node x\"`\n- **Context & Goal**: Implement first-class support for the official **X (formerly Twitter) Node** in the application\'s n8n workflow ecosystem (canvas, node library, automations page, templates, and execution pipeline).\n- **Core Success Criteria**:\n  1. Provide a fully interactive **X (Twitter) n8n Node** inside the workflow builder and node library (`n8n-nodes-base.x` / `n8n-nodes-base.twitter`).\n  2. Support key X operations: Post Tweet (text + media upload), Search Tweets, Reply to Tweet/Thread, Get User Profile, Like/Retweet, and Webhook/Stream Trigger on Tweet Created.\n  3. Support OAuth 2.0 / API Key & Bearer Token credentials configuration (API Key, API Secret Key, Access Token, Access Secret, Bearer Token).\n  4. Provide a pre-built, ready-to-run workflow template featuring Node X (e.g., *\"Social Orchestrator: Multi-Channel Post \342\206\222 X (Twitter) v2 API Publication with Media & Engagement Tracking\"*).\n  5. Include simulated execution test runner for Node X with live request/response JSON payload preview.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed in Previous Steps**:\n  - Full CI360 social publishing and n8n orchestration system running on Express + React (Vite).\n  - Editable team member profile photos with upload/presets (`TeamPage.tsx`, `Header.tsx`).\n  - Dedicated Direct n8n Login portal (`src/features/n8n/N8nDirectLoginPage.tsx`) with session handling in `server/src/app.ts` and `src/api/client.ts`.\n  - App compiles (`compile_applet`) and passes linter (`tsc --noEmit`).\n- **In Progress / Current Turn**:\n  - Inspected `/src` directories: `src/data/`, `src/types/`, `src/components/`, `src/features/`.\n  - Need to inspect existing workflow types and templates in `src/types/workflow.ts` and `src/data/templates.ts` to integrate the X Node smoothly into the existing canvas and template engine.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Decisions\n- **Existing Architecture**:\n  - Workflow templates reside in `src/data/templates.ts`.\n  - Node definitions and canvas types are in `src/types/workflow.ts` and components in `src/components/` (`WorkflowCanvas.tsx`, `NodeLibraryModal.tsx`).\n  - Backend has n8n webhook dispatcher and execution logger in `server/src/services/n8n/n8nService.ts` and `server/src/repositories/database.ts`.\n  - The application uses `x` as one of the active social platforms in analytics (`publishedByPlatform.x: 32`) and social accounts (`x.com`).\n- **Node X Specification**:\n  - Name: `X (Twitter)`\n  - Type identifier: `n8n-nodes-base.x` (or `n8n-nodes-base.twitter`)\n  - Icon: Official X mark (white/black minimalist X logo)\n  - Color accent: `#000000` / `#1DA1F2` (X dark slate / Twitter blue accent)\n  - Operations: `tweet:create` (Create Tweet), `tweet:search` (Search Recent Tweets), `tweet:reply` (Reply to Tweet), `user:get` (Get User Profile), `stream:trigger` (Stream Tweet Trigger).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- Port 3000 running Express + Vite dev server.\n- Navigation tabs currently supported: `\'overview\' | \'content\' | \'calendar\' | \'create\' | \'approvals\' | \'published\' | \'brands\' | \'accounts\' | \'automations\' | \'n8n-login\' | \'executions\' | \'analytics\' | \'sheets\' | \'team\' | \'audit\' | \'settings\'`.\n- All backend routes are operational; dev server is live.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n1. **View Existing Node & Template Definitions**:\n   - Check `src/types/workflow.ts` and `src/data/templates.ts` for node structure, inputs/outputs, parameter schemas.\n2. **Add X (Twitter) Node Definition**:\n   - Register the X Node in the node registry/library (`NodeLibraryModal.tsx` and node catalog in `src/data/` or `src/types/workflow.ts`).\n   - Define operations: Post Tweet, Search Tweets, Retweet/Like, Trigger on Mention.\n   - Define parameters: Tweet Text, Media URLs, Reply Settings, Geotargeting, Poll options, and OAuth 2.0 / Bearer token credential fields.\n3. **Add Dedicated Pre-Built X Workflow Template**:\n   - Create an end-to-end template in `src/data/templates.ts`:\n     `Webhook Trigger \342\206\222 AI Content Formatter \342\206\222 X (Twitter) v2 Node \342\206\222 Discord/Slack Notification`.\n4. **Interactive Node X Modal / Parameter Inspector**:\n   - In `WorkflowCanvas.tsx` or a dedicated Node X Configuration component, ensure clicking Node X opens its full properties panel with live execution testing.\n5. **Backend Simulation / Webhook Support**:\n   - In `server/src/services/n8n/n8nService.ts` and `server/src/repositories/database.ts`, support X node execution results (`perPlatformResults.x = { status: \'published\', tweetId: \'...\', url: \'https://x.com/status/...\' }`).\n6. **Verification**:\n   - Run `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` to ensure zero type errors, then restart dev server if server files change.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Keep styling aligned with Tailwind CSS and the existing modern dark/light UI.\n- No dummy/broken placeholders; all X node inputs (text, media, credentials, operations) must be functional, testable, and interactive.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 208
    included_step_index_end: 334
    user_requests: "all screen  responsive\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nMedia attachment: User sent attachment: /assets/aistudio/image_c98cab20.png (saved in workspace at /public/assets/aistudio/image_c98cab20.png). Read it with view_file at that path; in shell commands, which run from the workspace root, use the relative path public/assets/aistudio/image_c98cab20.png. When displaying or embedding this asset in code, reference this local file path directly. Only invoke image generation tools if the user explicitly requests creating or modifying an image.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
