  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Evaluating Component Quality**\n\nI\'ve been evaluating the quality of core n8n components. Specifically, I\'m finding that `WorkflowCanvas`, `NodeInspector`, `NodeLibraryModal`, `WebhookSandbox`, `JsonWorkflowModal`, and `DeveloperIntegrationsView` demonstrate a strong level of quality, especially regarding the visual flow builder. I\'m focusing on implementation details and user experience.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Canvas Access**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how users will access the visual workflow canvas, particularly with Node X in mind. I\'ve been examining `AutomationsPage.tsx`, which currently houses workflow cards and other features. My plan is to enhance it with a tab/mode switcher for better organization: \"Workflow Orchestrator\", \"n8n Visual Canvas & Node Builder\", \"Developer Integrations & Guides\", and \"Webhook Sandbox & Testing\". The \"n8n Visual Canvas\" tab will feature canvas controls and a prominent \"X (Twitter) v2 Social Orchestrator\" template.\n\n\n**Defining Node Interaction**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the interaction specifics of the Twitter/X v2 node. The goal is a highly intuitive configuration. I\'m focusing on an \"Operation Picker\" with options like `tweet:create` and `tweet:search`, and the credentials configuration. I\'m especially focused on the OAuth 2.0 implementation, with real-world test credentials pre-filled and a live \"Test Connection\" button. I\'m prioritizing dynamic operation parameters, like character counters for tweet text, and media attachment features.\n\n\n**Implementing Node Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing the advanced features of the Twitter/X v2 node. I\'m focusing on dynamic parameters, including reply settings and poll options. I\'m also ensuring a realistic test step execution. A JSON response structure from the Twitter API v2 will generate a live visual preview of the rendered Tweet card, alongside output JSON and a table view. I\'m also adding a new workflow to the database.\n\n\n**Defining Node Integrations**\n\nI\'m expanding the n8n platform to add `xNode` to `NodeType`. I am adding the `xNode` details to `NODE_DEFINITIONS`, with the action category and full operational/credential schemas. I\'m incorporating a Twitter/X trigger type when it fits. I am also making the \"X (Twitter) v2 Auto-Publisher & Thread Orchestrator\" template, and adding the required nodes. Further, I am incorporating the X icon into the `ICON_MAP`, and styling `xNode` with a dark theme and badge. The `NodeLibraryModal` is up next.\n\n\n**Integrating Node Components**\n\nI\'m now integrating the X icon mapping, and highlighting `X (Twitter)` within the action and social lists. I\'m building a full editor for `xNode` inside `NodeInspector`, with operations like \"Create Tweet\" and a live Tweet preview. I\'m incorporating a credential tester and status badge. Finally, I am adding a 280-character live counter with an overflow warning.\n\n\n"
