  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Workflow Editor**\n\nI\'m focusing on building the Workflow Editor tab, likely in `AutomationsPage.tsx` or a new component. My current thinking revolves around making it comprehensive. Users will select workflows (e.g., the \"X (Twitter) v2 Auto-Publisher & Thread Orchestrator\"), then be able to manipulate them: pan, zoom, drag nodes, and add new `xNode` instances.\n\n\n**Implementing Node Execution**\n\nNow I\'m diving into the execution engine. I\'m building out how individual nodes will run, including how they\'ll evaluate parameters and simulate responses. For instance, the `webhook` node will return the parsed `testPayload`, while `code` will execute custom JavaScript. I\'m also planning for nodes like `xNode`, `if`, and `httpRequest` to simulate the exact JSON responses.\n\n\n**Inspecting Node Details**\n\nI\'m now integrating the node inspector, focusing on the `xNode` type within `src/components/NodeInspector.tsx`. I\'ve reviewed the import statements and the custom `XIcon` for the header and tabs. I\'m focusing on making the input and output parameters visible to the user for inspection.\n\n\n**Refining Node Inspector**\n\nI\'m currently refining the `xNode` inspector, particularly the \"Parameters\" tab. I\'m fleshing out the specific operations: `createTweet`, `replyTweet`, `searchTweets`, `getUser`, `likeTweet`, and `retweet`. I\'m also working on the authentication details, covering different types like OAuth 2.0 and API Key/Secret. There\'s a \"Test Credentials\" button to verify these configurations, and I\'m ensuring all parameters are appropriately displayed for inspection.\n\n\n**Designing Tweet Node Preview**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive previews within the Tweet node inspector. For \'createTweet,\' I\'m designing a live mockup of the Twitter post, including the character counter, media previews, reply settings, and poll options. The \'replyTweet\' operation has its own live preview based on the parent tweet ID, tweet text, and an auto-quote toggle. In \'searchTweets\', I am implementing syntax suggestions.\n\n\n"
