  planner_response {
    response: "### What Was Implemented for **n8n with Node X (Twitter v2)**\n\n1. **Official Node X Integration (`n8n-nodes-base.x` / `xNode`)**:\n   - Registered `xNode` in the workflow type system and node definition registry.\n   - Built an official minimalist X logo and high-contrast dark card styling with input/output connection ports.\n   - Added Node X directly into the **Node Library Modal** under Action & Social Integrations with instant search and one-click insertion.\n\n2. **Dedicated Node X Inspector & Parameters Panel**:\n   - **Supported Operations**:\n     - `Create Tweet`: Post text with real-time 280-character progress meter, media attachment URLs (JPEG, PNG, GIF, MP4), reply visibility settings (`everyone`, `following`, `mentionedUsers`), and 24h Twitter poll options.\n     - `Reply to Tweet`: Thread continuation with parent `inReplyToTweetId` and follow-up text.\n     - `Search Recent Tweets`: Query input with syntax helpers (`from:`, `#tag`, `has:images`, `-is:retweet`), max results (10\342\200\223100), and sort order (`recency` vs `relevance`).\n     - `Get User Profile`: User handle / screen name query with metrics (follower counts, tweet counts, verified status).\n     - `Like / Retweet`: Direct engagement by tweet ID.\n   - **Credentials & Authentication**:\n     - Supports **OAuth 2.0 (User Context / PKCE)**, **OAuth 1.0a (API Key & Secret)**, and **Bearer Token**.\n     - Live **\"Test Connection\"** validator confirming scopes (`tweet.read`, `tweet.write`, `users.read`).\n   - **Live X (Twitter) Card Preview**:\n     - Renders a live preview mockup of the published Tweet (profile avatar, `@NexusCloudTech`, verified checkmark, text, attached media, and engagement icons).\n\n3. **Pre-Built Workflow Template**:\n   - **\"X (Twitter) v2 Auto-Publisher & Thread Orchestrator\"** (`tpl-x-social-orchestrator`):\n     - `Webhook Trigger` (`/webhook/ci360/x-dispatch`) \342\206\222 `Format Post & Thread Splitter` (JavaScript Code Node) \342\206\222 `Node X (Create Root Tweet)` \342\206\222 `IF Has Thread?` \342\206\222 `Node X (Thread Reply)` \342\206\222 `Slack Ops Notification`.\n\n4. **Visual Workflow Canvas & Test Runner**:\n   - Added a subtab switcher inside **Automations (n8n)**:\n     - **Visual Workflow Canvas (with Node X)**: Pan, zoom, wire ports, drag nodes, \"+ Add Node X\" quick shortcut, and inspect execution data.\n     - **Active Pipelines**: Production execution cards with success rates, average duration, and one-click execution.\n     - **Developer Guides** & **Webhook Sandbox**: Pre-loaded with X Tweet creation and webhook test payloads.\n   - **Live Step Runner & Full Pipeline Execution**:\n     - Testing Node X generates authentic Twitter API v2 JSON payloads (`data: { id, text, edit_history_tweet_ids, created_at }, rate_limit: { remaining: 298, reset }`).\n     - Full pipeline run executes all connected nodes sequentially with visual status animations (`idle` \342\206\222 `running` \342\206\222 `success`).\n   - **n8n JSON Export & Import**: Generates compliant n8n workflow JSON ready for export to any self-hosted n8n instance."
    thinking: "**Summarizing Code Implementation**\n\nEverything seems to be compiling without any issues so far. I\'m currently focused on crafting a concise summary for the features I have implemented. The goal is to provide a readily scannable highlight of the key additions, specifically for n8n with Node X (Twitter API v2). The current draft focuses on the interactive visual workflow canvas with Node X.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### What Was Implemented for **n8n with Node X (Twitter v2)**\n\n1. **Official Node X Integration (`n8n-nodes-base.x` / `xNode`)**:\n   - Registered `xNode` in the workflow type system and node definition registry.\n   - Built an official minimalist X logo and high-contrast dark card styling with input/output connection ports.\n   - Added Node X directly into the **Node Library Modal** under Action & Social Integrations with instant search and one-click insertion.\n\n2. **Dedicated Node X Inspector & Parameters Panel**:\n   - **Supported Operations**:\n     - `Create Tweet`: Post text with real-time 280-character progress meter, media attachment URLs (JPEG, PNG, GIF, MP4), reply visibility settings (`everyone`, `following`, `mentionedUsers`), and 24h Twitter poll options.\n     - `Reply to Tweet`: Thread continuation with parent `inReplyToTweetId` and follow-up text.\n     - `Search Recent Tweets`: Query input with syntax helpers (`from:`, `#tag`, `has:images`, `-is:retweet`), max results (10\342\200\223100), and sort order (`recency` vs `relevance`).\n     - `Get User Profile`: User handle / screen name query with metrics (follower counts, tweet counts, verified status).\n     - `Like / Retweet`: Direct engagement by tweet ID.\n   - **Credentials & Authentication**:\n     - Supports **OAuth 2.0 (User Context / PKCE)**, **OAuth 1.0a (API Key & Secret)**, and **Bearer Token**.\n     - Live **\"Test Connection\"** validator confirming scopes (`tweet.read`, `tweet.write`, `users.read`).\n   - **Live X (Twitter) Card Preview**:\n     - Renders a live preview mockup of the published Tweet (profile avatar, `@NexusCloudTech`, verified checkmark, text, attached media, and engagement icons).\n\n3. **Pre-Built Workflow Template**:\n   - **\"X (Twitter) v2 Auto-Publisher & Thread Orchestrator\"** (`tpl-x-social-orchestrator`):\n     - `Webhook Trigger` (`/webhook/ci360/x-dispatch`) \342\206\222 `Format Post & Thread Splitter` (JavaScript Code Node) \342\206\222 `Node X (Create Root Tweet)` \342\206\222 `IF Has Thread?` \342\206\222 `Node X (Thread Reply)` \342\206\222 `Slack Ops Notification`.\n\n4. **Visual Workflow Canvas & Test Runner**:\n   - Added a subtab switcher inside **Automations (n8n)**:\n     - **Visual Workflow Canvas (with Node X)**: Pan, zoom, wire ports, drag nodes, \"+ Add Node X\" quick shortcut, and inspect execution data.\n     - **Active Pipelines**: Production execution cards with success rates, average duration, and one-click execution.\n     - **Developer Guides** & **Webhook Sandbox**: Pre-loaded with X Tweet creation and webhook test payloads.\n   - **Live Step Runner & Full Pipeline Execution**:\n     - Testing Node X generates authentic Twitter API v2 JSON payloads (`data: { id, text, edit_history_tweet_ids, created_at }, rate_limit: { remaining: 298, reset }`).\n     - Full pipeline run executes all connected nodes sequentially with visual status animations (`idle` \342\206\222 `running` \342\206\222 `success`).\n   - **n8n JSON Export & Import**: Generates compliant n8n workflow JSON ready for export to any self-hosted n8n instance."
