  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Automation UI**\n\nI\'ve been examining lines 595-610 in `src/features/workflows/AutomationsPage.tsx`, specifically the UI rendering the \"Main Visual Canvas Box.\" I\'m diving deep into the component\'s structure, trying to understand how it\'s styled and arranged, especially considering the `relative`, `rounded-2xl`, `overflow-hidden`, and other classes. It\'s a key part of the automation interface, and my goal is to fully understand its visual behavior.\n\n\n**Examining Canvas Layout**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the immediate children within the \"Main Visual Canvas Box\", specifically the `WorkflowCanvas` and `NodeInspector` components. I\'m noting the `h-[580px]` and `lg:min-h-[640px]` styles. The relationship between these two components, particularly how the `NodeInspector` is positioned relative to the `WorkflowCanvas`, is of interest.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Height Issue**\n\nI\'ve isolated a critical CSS behavior: when the parent container lacks an explicit `height` but has `min-height`, children with `height: 100%` don\'t inherit the `min-height` value, resulting in zero content height for `WorkflowCanvas`! This explains the empty canvas observed. Replacing `min-h-[580px]` with `h-[620px] w-full` immediately resolved the issue by explicitly setting the height. I\'ve also noted that the initial value of `selectedNodeId` is responsible for causing the NodeInspector to be open on page load.\n\n\n**Refining Node Interaction**\n\nI\'ve been improving node interactions. Setting `selectedNodeId` to `null` initially creates a full-width canvas with all nodes beautifully displayed. I added a button to the toolbar that quickly selects the first node if `xNode` isn\'t found, and clicking a node correctly opens the inspector within the canvas container. The \"Configure Node X\" button is now fully functional!\n\n\n"
