  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Node Selection**\n\nI\'ve realized that the `handleNodeMouseDown` function is responsible for node selection, calling `onSelectNode(node.id)`. Now, I\'m thinking about how to deselect the node when the canvas background is clicked. `handleMouseDown` already seems to handle this with `onSelectNode(null)`, so I should confirm the behavior and integrate it effectively.\n\n\n**Refining Node Interaction**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that clicking the canvas background deselects nodes, thanks to `onSelectNode(null)` in `handleMouseDown`. Now, I\'m working on how this integrates within the `AutomationsPage.tsx` file. I\'m updating the `selectedNodeId` state to initialize as `null` and adjusting the canvas container\'s dimensions for better display. I\'ve also implemented a \"Configure Node X\" toolbar button for easier node configuration.\n\n\n"
