  planner_response {
    response: "### Summary of Fixes\n\nThe issue shown in your screenshot has been resolved:\n\n1. **Fixed Canvas Height & Visibility**:\n   - The canvas container previously had `min-h-[580px]` with no explicit height, which caused child layers with `height: 100%` (`h-full`) to collapse to `0px` in the browser because all workflow nodes are absolutely positioned.\n   - Set the canvas viewport to an explicit `h-[640px] w-full`, allowing all nodes, connection wires, ports, and controls to render immediately.\n\n2. **Contained the Node Inspector to the Canvas**:\n   - The inspector panel was previously using viewport `fixed inset-y-0 right-0`, which caused it to span from the very top of the window to the bottom, covering the application header, brand dropdown, search bar, and page tabs.\n   - Changed the inspector to `absolute inset-y-0 right-0 z-30` constrained strictly within the canvas container. The top navigation, page title, and tabs remain clear and unobstructed.\n\n3. **Restored Full Canvas View on Load**:\n   - Initialized `selectedNodeId` to `null` on load so the full workflow graph (`Webhook` \342\206\222 `Code Formatter` \342\206\222 `Node X` \342\206\222 `IF Condition` \342\206\222 `Node X Thread Reply` \342\206\222 `Slack Notification`) is immediately visible with its connecting wires.\n   - Added a **\"Configure Node X\"** button in the canvas toolbar alongside the **\"+ Node X\"** shortcut, allowing you to open and test the Twitter/X v2 node whenever needed.\n   - Clicking any node or port on the canvas opens its respective configuration panel. Clicking `X` closes it.\n\n4. **Added n8n Canvas Dot Grid & Default Zoom**:\n   - Configured `.canvas-dot-grid` background styling in `index.css`.\n   - Adjusted initial canvas zoom to `0.85` and centered node coordinates so all workflow nodes fit within the viewing area."
    thinking: "**Clarifying the Fix**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the root cause! The canvas wrapper\'s `min-h-[580px]` combined with no fixed height was collapsing the child canvas (with `h-full`) to zero height. This explains why the user saw an empty or collapsed canvas, even though its internal layers were present.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Summary of Fixes\n\nThe issue shown in your screenshot has been resolved:\n\n1. **Fixed Canvas Height & Visibility**:\n   - The canvas container previously had `min-h-[580px]` with no explicit height, which caused child layers with `height: 100%` (`h-full`) to collapse to `0px` in the browser because all workflow nodes are absolutely positioned.\n   - Set the canvas viewport to an explicit `h-[640px] w-full`, allowing all nodes, connection wires, ports, and controls to render immediately.\n\n2. **Contained the Node Inspector to the Canvas**:\n   - The inspector panel was previously using viewport `fixed inset-y-0 right-0`, which caused it to span from the very top of the window to the bottom, covering the application header, brand dropdown, search bar, and page tabs.\n   - Changed the inspector to `absolute inset-y-0 right-0 z-30` constrained strictly within the canvas container. The top navigation, page title, and tabs remain clear and unobstructed.\n\n3. **Restored Full Canvas View on Load**:\n   - Initialized `selectedNodeId` to `null` on load so the full workflow graph (`Webhook` \342\206\222 `Code Formatter` \342\206\222 `Node X` \342\206\222 `IF Condition` \342\206\222 `Node X Thread Reply` \342\206\222 `Slack Notification`) is immediately visible with its connecting wires.\n   - Added a **\"Configure Node X\"** button in the canvas toolbar alongside the **\"+ Node X\"** shortcut, allowing you to open and test the Twitter/X v2 node whenever needed.\n   - Clicking any node or port on the canvas opens its respective configuration panel. Clicking `X` closes it.\n\n4. **Added n8n Canvas Dot Grid & Default Zoom**:\n   - Configured `.canvas-dot-grid` background styling in `index.css`.\n   - Adjusted initial canvas zoom to `0.85` and centered node coordinates so all workflow nodes fit within the viewing area."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 898791446
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
