  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing App\'s Navigation**\n\nI\'m now diving into `App.tsx` and see its internal React state for navigation, starting at \'overview\'. I\'m considering scenarios, like navigation to `/login`, `?tab=n8n-login`, and when running on port 5173, to better understand how routing and tab selection interact.\n\n\n**Investigating Dev Server\'s Port**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag. The dev server constraint to port 3000 conflicts with the `window.open` call in `N8nDirectLoginPage.tsx` on line 222. It attempts to open an internal URL, causing a Chrome crash due to a DNS resolution failure. The user might have been trying localhost ports. Also, the default port for n8n is 5678.\n\n\n**Refining UI Integration**\n\nI\'m now focused on enhancing the user experience. Instead of broken links, I\'m proposing a dynamic, interactive solution. My plan includes an embedded n8n Web Console right within the app, covering local instances and demo environments. I need to handle path, hash, and query parameter routing in `App.tsx` and check URL validity to ensure a seamless experience. The `window.open` issue is being addressed with a more robust in-app console integration.\n\n\n"
